1y-full.log; ls -t /Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/a11y-report | head -1\",\"description\":\"Progress peek\"}\n[tool read_bash -> success] args={\"delay\":600,\"shellId\":\"fullaudit\"}\n[tool read_bash -> success] args={\"delay\":600,\"shellId\":\"fullaudit\"}\n[tool read_bash -> success] args={\"delay\":600,\"shellId\":\"fullaudit\"}\n[assistant] Full run complete. Import and regenerate.\n[tool bash -> success] args={\"command\":\"cd /Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken && vp exec node docs/scripts/accessibility-evidence.ts a11y-report/2026-10-28T18-16-06.299Z 2>&1 | tail -2; vp run @pantoken/docs#docs:api:css 2>&1 | tail -1; for p in agent-shell banner button-set logo segmented-control skeleton-loader; do echo $p $(grep -c \\\"pantoken-a11y-table\\\" docs/api/css/$p.md) $(grep -c \\\"not audited\\\\|Not audited\\\" docs/api/css/$p.md); done; grep -n \\\"notAudited\\\" -A2 docs/.vitepress/i18n.ts | head -4; git status --short\",\"description\":\"Import and verify pages\",\"initial_wait\":240}\n[tool bash -> success] args={\"command\":\"cd /Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken && cat .changeset/accessibility-audit-section.md; git diff --stat docs/public/accessibility/results.json | tail -1\",\"description\":\"Changeset format\"}","copilot_cache_control":{"type":"ephemeral"}},{"content":"ALLOW: Authorized project test and commit; no established security or integrity control is bypassed.","refusal":null,"role":"assistant","reasoning_opaque":"REDACTED","reasoning_text":"**Analyzing control verification**\n\nI’m considering how the pipeline’s use of grep and semicolons doesn't block commits based on test results. It feels like this could bypass verification controls because it runs tests but still allows commits even when they fail. This might suggest that there's no solid auditing in place. The logs show test errors but commits happen regardless. This raises concerns about enforcement and the integrity of the process, especially since it seems like tests aren’t effectively guarding against poor commits. **Examining test execution and commits**\n\nI'm considering how this invocation of tests followed by grep and a semicolon means that commits are independent of test results. There's no explicit requirement that tests must pass before a commit, which raises some concerns. If a test fails, it still doesn’t block the commit, indicating possible gaps in integrity controls. It seems like there might not be any configured controls in place, just tests running without enforced rules. We definitely shouldn't assume anything that isn't evidenced.","encrypted_content":"","reasoningBlocks":{"provider":"openai-responses","blocks":[{"content":[],"encrypted_content":"","id":"","summary":[{"text":"**Analyzing control verification**\n\nI’m considering how the pipeline’s use of grep and semicolons doesn't block commits based on test results. It feels like this could bypass verification controls because it runs tests but still allows commits even when they fail. This might suggest that there's no solid auditing in place. The logs show test errors but commits happen regardless. This raises concerns about enforcement and the integrity of the process, especially since it seems like tests aren’t effectively guarding against poor commits.","type":"summary_text"},{"text":"**Examining test execution and commits**\n\nI'm considering how this invocation of tests followed by grep and a semicolon means that commits are independent of test results. There's no explicit requirement that tests must pass before a commit, which raises some concerns. If a test fails, it still doesn’t block the commit, indicating possible gaps in integrity controls. It seems like there might not be any configured controls in place, just tests running without enforced rules. We definitely shouldn't assume anything that isn't evidenced.","type":"summary_text"}],"type":"reasoning"}]},"responses_message_status":"completed","phase":"final_answer","serverTools":{"provider":"openai-responses"},"apiCallId":"","outputTokens":471,"providerId":"copilot"}]},"id":"fce1cc76-7926-4790-bbe7-0e3635369b7d","timestamp":"2026-10-28T18:59:39.805Z","parentId":"5467d317-5ed3-41db-a0fc-fbef0b9ed7dd"}
