{"type":"assistant.message","data":{"messageId":"1b06e97c-133d-40ef-8e72-a38eac0b3cfc","originatingMessageId":"73c76ac7-38c1-4a1e-a8f8-81f01d04ec99","model":"claude-sonnet-5.5","providerId":"copilot","content":"","toolRequests":[{"toolCallId":"toolu_01Ue3dUm1cZESqnR5s6Jwryk","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken && head -5 docs/api/css/color.md docs/api/css/primitives.md docs/api/css/base.md docs/api/css/breakpoints.md docs/api/css/maskglobal.md | cut -c1-200; cat formats/components/src/rules/index.ts | grep -v \"^ \\*\\|^/\\*\" ; cat formats/components/src/declarations/index.ts | grep -v \"^ \\*\\|^/\\*\"; cd formats/components/src; for f in utilities/*/*.css rules/*/*.css declarations/*/*.css; do echo \"$f a11y=$(grep -c '@a11y\\|@accessibility' $f) ex=$(grep -c '@example' $f) auto=$(grep -c automatica11y $f)\"; done","description":"Survey records for a11y and examples"},"type":"function","intentionSummary":"Survey records for a11y and examples","toolTitle":"Running command"}],"interactionId":"b4f03ceb-0b21-44ca-9a3e-694263c338bd","turnId":"1","reasoningOpaque":"REDACTED","reasoningText":"I'm noting which parts remain unaudited—several core utilities, rule files, declarations, and a couple of components like ai-gradient and segmented-control—and realizing I need to check those specific records to decide how \"where applicable\" should be interpreted for each.\n\nNow I'm thinking through a11y relevance per item: many utilities like gap or spacing are purely visual with no accessibility angle, while others like transition (reduced motion), truncate (clipped text), overflow (keyboard scroll access), position/stacking (overlap), responsive (hidden content), text spacing, and contrast-related pieces (prose, base, ai-gradient) clearly warrant scrutiny. I still need to check what the color and primitives pages actually cover, and verify whether the existing guard test only checks components and focus state rather than these broader utility concerns.","rte":true,"apiCallId":"msg_011CgVAHeuVAAUdTrGwS8sdT","reasoningBlocks":{"provider":"anthropic-messages","blocks":[{"signature":"","thinking":"I'm noting which parts remain unaudited—several core utilities, rule files, declarations, and a couple of components like ai-gradient and segmented-control—and realizing I need to check those specific records to decide how \"where applicable\" should be interpreted for each.\n\nNow I'm thinking through a11y relevance per item: many utilities like gap or spacing are purely visual with no accessibility angle, while others like transition (reduced motion), truncate (clipped text), overflow (keyboard scroll access), position/stacking (overlap), responsive (hidden content), text spacing, and contrast-related pieces (prose, base, ai-gradient) clearly warrant scrutiny. I still need to check what the color and primitives pages actually cover, and verify whether the existing guard test only checks components and focus state rather than these broader utility concerns.\n\n","type":"thinking"}]}},"id":"2275a53e-bfa9-4e7e-b61d-47cf006f4532","timestamp":"2026-10-28T19:08:25.031Z","parentId":"aade6548-7207-4ceb-bafe-6606c3517d24"}
{"type":"tool.execution_start","data":{"toolCallId":"toolu_01Ue3dUm1cZESqnR5s6Jwryk","toolName":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken && head -5 docs/api/css/color.md docs/api/css/primitives.md docs/api/css/base.md docs/api/css/breakpoints.md docs/api/css/maskglobal.md | cut -c1-200; cat formats/components/src/rules/index.ts | grep -v \"^ \\*\\|^/\\*\" ; cat formats/components/src/declarations/index.ts | grep -v \"^ \\*\\|^/\\*\"; cd formats/components/src; for f in utilities/*/*.css rules/*/*.css declarations/*/*.css; do echo \"$f a11y=$(grep -c '@a11y\\|@accessibility' $f) ex=$(grep -c '@example' $f) auto=$(grep -c automatica11y $f)\"; done","description":"Survey records for a11y and examples"},"turnId":"1","model":"claude-sonnet-5.5","toolTitle":"Running command","shellToolInfo":{"possiblePaths":["utilities/*/*.css","rules/*/*.css","declarations/*/*.css","/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken","docs/api/css/color.md","docs/api/css/primitives.md","docs/api/css/base.md","docs/api/css/breakpoints.md","docs/api/css/maskglobal.md","formats/components/src/rules/index.ts","formats/components/src/declarations/index.ts","formats/components/src","$f"],"hasWriteFileRedirection":false}},"id":"512f37ac-660d-44e0-a4b5-dad7e107390e","timestamp":"2026-10-28T19:08:25.054Z","parentId":"2275a53e-bfa9-4e7e-b61d-47cf006f4532"}
