{"type":"assistant.message","data":{"messageId":"455f9ff7-7559-45ca-a009-176ac9de0099","originatingMessageId":"73c76ac7-38c1-4a1e-a8f8-81f01d04ec99","model":"claude-sonnet-5.5","providerId":"copilot","content":"","toolRequests":[{"toolCallId":"toolu_01QA9ZhatrdnwGhhk98aKnsV","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src && ls utilities/spacing utilities/transition utilities/truncate; sed -n 1,60p utilities/truncate/index.ts; sed -n 1,40p utilities/transition/transition.css; grep -n \"color\" ../scripts/generate.ts | head -20; sed -n 1,80p lib/define.ts | head -90","description":"See how utility records are authored"},"type":"function","intentionSummary":"See how utility records are authored","toolTitle":"Running command"}],"interactionId":"b4f03ceb-0b21-44ca-9a3e-694263c338bd","turnId":"3","reasoningOpaque":"REDACTED","reasoningText":"I'm noting that some pages lack accessibility sections while others don't, likely depending on how the docs get generated, and I'm compiling the list of applicable pages like transition, visual-debug, base, prose, truncate, overflow, spacing, layout, responsive, position, stacking, cursor, gap, and mask.\n\nI'm settling on a plan: add automated accessibility examples and annotations for transition, visual-debug, base, prose, truncate, overflow, spacing, gap, layout, responsive, position, stacking, cursor, mask, ai-gradient, and color, while skipping elevation, breakpoints, primitives, segmented-control.segment, logos, and layouts since they're either decorative, arbitrary, or already covered elsewhere. I also need to dedupe the definitions list since icon and screen-reader-content already appear in COMPONENTS.\n\nNow I'm checking how color utilities are actually generated versus the other records, since they don't appear in the UTILITIES list the same way — I need to trace how transition and spacing records are authored to figure out the right pattern for color.","rte":true,"apiCallId":"msg_011CgVAKQ177Tk4vKN49R3Dw","reasoningBlocks":{"provider":"anthropic-messages","blocks":[{"signature":"","thinking":"I'm noting that some pages lack accessibility sections while others don't, likely depending on how the docs get generated, and I'm compiling the list of applicable pages like transition, visual-debug, base, prose, truncate, overflow, spacing, layout, responsive, position, stacking, cursor, gap, and mask.\n\nI'm settling on a plan: add automated accessibility examples and annotations for transition, visual-debug, base, prose, truncate, overflow, spacing, gap, layout, responsive, position, stacking, cursor, mask, ai-gradient, and color, while skipping elevation, breakpoints, primitives, segmented-control.segment, logos, and layouts since they're either decorative, arbitrary, or already covered elsewhere. I also need to dedupe the definitions list since icon and screen-reader-content already appear in COMPONENTS.\n\nNow I'm checking how color utilities are actually generated versus the other records, since they don't appear in the UTILITIES list the same way — I need to trace how transition and spacing records are authored to figure out the right pattern for color.\n\n","type":"thinking"}]}},"id":"b6ff47e3-eb35-4ce3-ac7c-65f6ef747faf","timestamp":"2026-10-28T19:08:50.842Z","parentId":"55dc2be8-6ed0-4bfc-b1d8-5b98fc4af181"}
