ample, plus integration work. I'm being pragmatic about it, starting by figuring out which utilities actually affect accessibility checks—like truncate, which clips text and relates to reflow and content-loss concerns, and overflow, where scrollable regions need keyboard focusability.\n\nI'm also considering spacing, gap, layout, responsive visibility, position, stacking, cursor, mask/overlay, transition, visual-debug, base, prose, and ai-gradient utilities for similar treatment. For color, I'm unsure whether it belongs in the main UTILITIES list or is handled separately in generate.ts, so I want to check that—color utilities are highly relevant to accessibility since they tie directly into contrast requirements, so I should trace how the color record gets generated before deciding how to handle it.\n\n","type":"thinking"}]}},"id":"5b2d1545-b3ac-45c3-9921-bca1dfe8ed47","timestamp":"2026-10-28T19:09:02.740Z","parentId":"29aac776-739e-4182-8d22-2967cc26ad23"}
