ed version to make sure the audit script references every utility name correctly, not just a partial set.\n\nSince ai-gradient is registered separately in the plugin as well as core, and names must be unique in the snapshot, I'll go with auditing the core version and adding the a11y example there, while mirroring the guidance into the plugin source for consistency even though only the core one will actually be scored. Now I'm going through each file to insert the a11y examples — starting with the truncate component, where I'll add the accessibility example near the existing button example, placed before the related-text line.","rte":true,"apiCallId":"msg_011CgVAPvdx8spReHGde1tsG","reasoningBlocks":{"provider":"anthropic-messages","blocks":[{"signature":"","thinking":"I notice ai-gradient isn't showing up in the UTILITIES list, so I need to pull the full list rather than the truncated version to make sure the audit script references every utility name correctly, not just a partial set.\n\nSince ai-gradient is registered separately in the plugin as well as core, and names must be unique in the snapshot, I'll go with auditing the core version and adding the a11y example there, while mirroring the guidance into the plugin source for consistency even though only the core one will actually be scored. Now I'm going through each file to insert the a11y examples — starting with the truncate component, where I'll add the accessibility example near the existing button example, placed before the related-text line.\n\n","type":"thinking"}]}},"id":"a776e0ae-26f4-4a31-9fc6-509d06518fb5","timestamp":"2026-10-28T19:09:52.087Z","parentId":"d9732949-f1a4-4eac-bbad-05992d4c55f7"}
