ipts/audit-plugin-components.ts`. - **agent-shell:** it was the only one of the six missing guidance, so I added an `@a11y` block and an `-automatica11y` example (a labelled `<section>`). The other five already had both. - **Guard test:** a new test requires every plugin record to have `@a11y` text and an audit example. - **Snapshot:** I re-ran the whole audit and re-imported it. The snapshot went from 76 to 82 records. A few things you might trip over: - **Left out:** the plugin's `ai-gradient` is still unaudited. It's a utility, not a component, and it has no `@a11y` text or examples. It also has the same name as a core record. Say if you want it included. `card` was already covered through core, and `segmented-control.segment` has no page of its own. - **Not covered:** the layouts plugin pages (callout, hero and similar) are still \"Not audited\", per your choice of custom-components only. - **Changeset:** I added one for `@pantoken/plugin-custom-components`. It covers the `agent-shell` guidance. - **Snapshot diff:** the snapshot file shows a large diff because the full run replaced all of its contents. - **CI:** I haven't re-run it on any of these changes.\n[human #20] layout plugin doesn't need to be covered. for both components and custom-components go through the utilities, declarations, etc. and add those audits where applicable.\n[context] <current_datetime>2026-10-28T13:08:05.474-06:00</current_datetime> layout plugin doesn't need to be covered. for both components and custom-components go through the utilities, declarations, etc. and add those audits where applicable.\n[tool bash -> success] args={\"command\":\"cd /Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken && grep -L \\\"pantoken-a11y-table\\\" docs/api/css/*.md | xargs -n1 basename; sed -n 1,60p formats/components/src/components/index.ts | head -60; cat formats/components/src/utilities/index.ts | head -40; ls formats/components/src/declarations plugins/pantoken/custom-components/src/declarations\",\"description\":\"List unaudited pages and source buckets\"}\n[tool bash -> success] args={\"command\":\"cd /Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken && head -5 docs/api/css/color.md docs/api/css/primitives.md docs/api/css/base.md docs/api/css/breakpoints.md docs/api/css/maskglobal.md | cut -c1-200; cat formats/components/src/rules/index.ts | grep -v \\\"^ \\\\*\\\\|^/\\\\*\\\" ; cat formats/components/src/declarations/index.ts | grep -v \\\"^ \\\\*\\\\|^/\\\\*\\\"; cd formats/components/src; for f in utilities/*/*.css rules/*/*.css declarations/*/*.css; do echo \\\"$f a11y=$(grep -c '@a11y\\\\|@accessibility' $f) ex=$(grep -c '@example' $f) auto=$(grep -c automatica11y $f)\\\"; done\",\"description\":\"Survey records for a11y and examples\"}\n[tool bash -> success] args={\"command\":\"cd /Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components && cat > /tmp/survey.ts <<'E'\\nimport { parseCssDocs } from \\\"@cssdoc/core\\\";\\nimport { UTILITIES } from \\\"/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/utilities/index.ts\\\";\\nimport { RULES } from \\\"/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/rules/index.ts\\\";\\nimport { DECLARATIONS } from \\\"/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/declarations/index.ts\\\";\\nimport { resolveExampleTargets } from \\\"@pantoken/utils/example-targets\\\";\\nfor (const [k, list] of [[\\\"util\\\", UTILITIES], [\\\"rule\\\", RULES], [\\\"decl\\\", DECLARATIONS]] as const)\\n for (const r of list) {\\n const es = parseCssDocs(r.rules(\\\"instui-\\\")).filter((e) => e.name === r.name);\\n const e = es[0];\\n console.log(k, r.name, \\\"entries\\\", es.length, \\\"a11y\\\", !!e?.accessibility?.trim(), \\\"ex\\\", e?.examples.length, \\\"auto\\\", e ? resolveExampleTargets(e.examples).automatica11y.length : \\\"-\\\");\\n }\\nE\\ncp /tmp/survey.ts scripts/_survey.ts && node scripts/_survey.ts 2>&1 | tail -30; rm scripts/_survey.ts\",\"description\":\"Survey utility/rule/declaration records\"}\n[tool bash -> success] args={\"command\":\"cd /Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src && ls utilities/spacing utilities/transition utilities/truncate; sed -n 1,60p utilities/truncate/index.ts; sed -n 1,40p utilities/transition/transition.css; grep -n \\\"color\\\" ../scripts/generate.ts | head -20; sed -n 1,80p lib/define.ts | head -90\",\"description\":\"See how utility records are authored\"}\n[tool bash -> success] args={\"command\":\"cd /Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/utilities && sed -n 10,60p truncate/index.ts; echo ======; sed -n 1,40p transition/transition.css\",\"description\":\"Truncate and transition\"}\n[tool bash -> success] args={\"command\":\"cd /Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken && grep -rn \\\"@utility color\\\\|@component color\\\\|--text-danger\\\" --include=*.ts formats/components/src formats/components/scripts -l | head; sed -n 1,30p docs/api/css/color.md | cut -c1-300\",\"description\":\"Locate color record\"}\n[tool bash -> success] args={\"command\":\"cd /Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components && grep -n \\\"@utility color\\\" -B12 -A25 scripts/generate.ts | head -90\",\"description\":\"Color record in generate.ts\"}","copilot_cache_control":{"type":"ephemeral"}},{"content":"ALLOW: Adds relevant accessibility guidance and test example within the requested project scope.","refusal":null,"role":"assistant","reasoning_opaque":"REDACTED","reasoning_text":"","encrypted_content":"REDACTED","reasoningBlocks":{"provider":"openai-responses","blocks":[{"content":[],"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"","summary":[],"type":"reasoning"}]},"responses_message_status":"completed","phase":"final_answer","serverTools":{"provider":"openai-responses"},"apiCallId":"","outputTokens":114,"providerId":"copilot"}]},"id":"e4d702d3-a4fb-457b-a503-8f89369c45af","timestamp":"2026-10-28T19:10:16.516Z","parentId":"7d5a0c97-5584-420a-b72d-3d570791766b"}
{"type":"permission.requested","data":{"requestId":"8994a375-e802-42d5-b421-38a90f40e343","permissionRequest":{"kind":"write","toolCallId":"toolu_01LTXgJgfwXvTwG9eeDnum1D","intention":"Edit file","fileName":"/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/utilities/cursor/index.ts","diff":"\ndiff --git a/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/utilities/cursor/index.ts b/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/utilities/cursor/index.ts\nindex 0000000..0000000 100644\n--- a/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/utilities/cursor/index.ts\n+++ b/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/utilities/cursor/index.ts\n@@ -49,6 +49,11 @@\n  * @modifier --cursor-move — cursor: move.\n  * @modifier --cursor-grab — cursor: grab.\n  * @modifier --cursor-wait — cursor: wait.\n+ * @a11y The cursor only affects pointer users; a pointer cursor doesn't make an element operable. Put it on native controls (\\`button\\`, \\`a\\`), and never use \\`--cursor-not-allowed\\` or \\`--cursor-wait\\` as the only sign that something is disabled or busy.\n+ * @example -automatica11y\n+ * \\`\\`\\`html\n+ * <button class=\"instui-button --cursor-pointer\">Open details</button>\n+ * \\`\\`\\`\n  * @example\n  * <div class=\"--cursor-pointer\">…</div>\n  */\n","newFileContents":"/**\n * The cursor utility — CSS `cursor` as composable, globally-available classes (bare, or chained onto\n * any component) — copied from `view`'s former `-cursor-*` modifiers.\n *\n * @module\n */\nimport { css } from \"../../lib/css.ts\";\nimport { defineUtility, type Definition } from \"../../lib/define.ts\";\nimport { globalModifierSelector } from \"@pantoken/utils\";\n\nconst CURSORS = [\n  \"auto\",\n  \"default\",\n  \"pointer\",\n  \"not-allowed\",\n  \"text\",\n  \"move\",\n  \"grab\",\n  \"wait\",\n] as const;\n\n/** Build CSS rules for a property/value map. Helper for cursor/position utilities. */\nconst buildPropertyRules = (\n  p: string,\n  prefix: string,\n  property: string,\n  values: readonly string[],\n): string[] =>\n  values.map(\n    (value) => `${globalModifierSelector(p, `${prefix}-${value}`)} { ${property}: ${value}; }`,\n  );\n\n/** The cursor utility — `cursor` as composable, global classes. */\nexport const cursor: Definition = defineUtility({\n  name: \"cursor\",\n  css: (p) => {\n    const rules = buildPropertyRules(p, \"cursor\", \"cursor\", Array.from(CURSORS));\n    // prettier-ignore\n    return css`/**\n * @utility cursor\n * @selector .--cursor-pointer\n * @global\n * @summary \\`cursor\\` as a composable, global class — \\`.--cursor-<value>\\` — usable bare or chained onto any component (\\`.instui-button.--cursor-pointer\\`).\n * @modifier --cursor-auto — cursor: auto.\n * @modifier --cursor-default — cursor: default.\n * @modifier --cursor-pointer — cursor: pointer.\n * @modifier --cursor-not-allowed — cursor: not-allowed.\n * @modifier --cursor-text — cursor: text.\n * @modifier --cursor-move — cursor: move.\n * @modifier --cursor-grab — cursor: grab.\n * @modifier --cursor-wait — cursor: wait.\n * @a11y The cursor only affects pointer users; a pointer cursor doesn't make an element operable. Put it on native controls (\\`button\\`, \\`a\\`), and never use \\`--cursor-not-allowed\\` or \\`--cursor-wait\\` as the only sign that something is disabled or busy.\n * @example -automatica11y\n * \\`\\`\\`html\n * <button class=\"instui-button --cursor-pointer\">Open details</button>\n * \\`\\`\\`\n * @example\n * <div class=\"--cursor-pointer\">…</div>\n */\n${rules.join(\"\\n\")}`;\n  },\n});\n\n/** The cursor utility as a standalone, header-wrapped stylesheet. */\nexport const cursorUtilitiesCss: Definition[\"css\"] = cursor.css;\n","canOfferSessionApproval":true,"fileEdits":[{"before":{"path":"/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/utilities/cursor/index.ts","content":"/**\n * The cursor utility — CSS `cursor` as composable, globally-available classes (bare, or chained onto\n * any