ipts/audit-plugin-components.ts`. - **agent-shell:** it was the only one of the six missing guidance, so I added an `@a11y` block and an `-automatica11y` example (a labelled `<section>`). The other five already had both. - **Guard test:** a new test requires every plugin record to have `@a11y` text and an audit example. - **Snapshot:** I re-ran the whole audit and re-imported it. The snapshot went from 76 to 82 records. A few things you might trip over: - **Left out:** the plugin's `ai-gradient` is still unaudited. It's a utility, not a component, and it has no `@a11y` text or examples. It also has the same name as a core record. Say if you want it included. `card` was already covered through core, and `segmented-control.segment` has no page of its own. - **Not covered:** the layouts plugin pages (callout, hero and similar) are still \"Not audited\", per your choice of custom-components only. - **Changeset:** I added one for `@pantoken/plugin-custom-components`. It covers the `agent-shell` guidance. - **Snapshot diff:** the snapshot file shows a large diff because the full run replaced all of its contents. - **CI:** I haven't re-run it on any of these changes.\n[human #20] layout plugin doesn't need to be covered. for both components and custom-components go through the utilities, declarations, etc. and add those audits where applicable.\n[context] <current_datetime>2026-10-28T13:08:05.474-06:00</current_datetime> layout plugin doesn't need to be covered. for both components and custom-components go through the utilities, declarations, etc. and add those audits where applicable.\n[tool bash -> success] args={\"command\":\"cd /Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken && grep -L \\\"pantoken-a11y-table\\\" docs/api/css/*.md | xargs -n1 basename; sed -n 1,60p formats/components/src/components/index.ts | head -60; cat formats/components/src/utilities/index.ts | head -40; ls formats/components/src/declarations plugins/pantoken/custom-components/src/declarations\",\"description\":\"L