Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken && vp test run docs/scripts/accessibility-evidence.test.ts 2>&1 | grep -E \\\"AssertionError|Error|expected|❯ docs\\\" | head; grep -n \\\"checked-in evidence has supported\\\" -A40 docs/scripts/accessibility-evidence.test.ts | head -60\",\"description\":\"Inspect failing test\",\"initial_wait\":90}\n[tool edit -> success] args={\"new_str\":\" expect(Object.keys(snapshot.records)).toHaveLength(82);\",\"old_str\":\" expect(Object.keys(snapshot.records)).toHaveLength(76);\",\"path\":\"/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/docs/scripts/accessibility-evidence.test.ts\"}\n[tool edit -> success] args={\"new_str\":\" expect(snapshot.records[\\\"agent-shell\\\"]).toHaveLength(4);\\n expect(snapshot.records[\\\"ai-gradient\\\"]).toBeUndefined();\",\"old_str\":\" expect(snapshot.records[\\\"agent-shell\\\"]).toBeUndefined();\",\"path\":\"/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/docs/scripts/accessibility-evidence.test.ts\"}\n[tool bash -> success] args={\"command\":\"cd /Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken && vp test run docs/scripts/accessibility-evidence.test.ts 2>&1 | grep -E \\\"Tests |FAIL|Assertion\\\"; git add -- docs/scripts/accessibility-evidence.test.ts && git commit -q -m \\\"test(docs): expect the custom components in the snapshot\\\" -m \\\"Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\\\" 2>&1 | tail -1; git log --oneline -1\",\"description\":\"Fix and commit test\",\"initial_wait\":120}\n[assistant] `agent-shell` and five other custom-components records are now audited, and their API pages show real audit tables instead of \"Not audited\". I did not look at the pages in a browser. The full audit and the importer tests pass. - **What was wrong:** the audit only covered the core records, so none of the plugin components were ever included. - **What's now covered:** `agent-shell`, `banner`, `button-set`, `logo`, `segmented-control` and `skeleton-loader`. The pages load the plugin's stylesheet, and the list lives in `formats/components/scripts/audit-plugin-components.ts`. - **agent-shell:** it was the only one of the six missing guidance, so I added an `@a11y` block and an `-automatica11y` example (a labelled `<section>`). The other five already had both. - **Guard test:** a new test requires every plugin record to have `@a11y` text and an audit example. - **Snapshot:** I re-ran the whole audit and re-imported it. The snapshot went from 76 to 82 records. A few things you might trip over: - **Left out:** the plugin's `ai-gradient` is still unaudited. It's a utility, not a component, and it has no `@a11y` text or examples. It also has the same name as a core record. Say if you want it included. `card` was already covered through core, and `segmented-control.segment` has no page of its own. - **Not covered:** the layouts plugin pages (callout, hero and similar) are still \"Not audited\", per your choice of custom-components only. - **Changeset:** I added one for `@pantoken/plugin-custom-components`. It covers the `agent-shell` guidance. - **Snapshot diff:** the snapshot file shows a large diff because the full run replaced all of its contents. - **CI:** I haven't re-run it on any of these changes.\n[human #20] layout plugin doesn't need to be covered. for both components and custom-components go through the utilities, declarations, etc. and add those audits where applicable.\n[context] <current_datetime>2026-10-28T13:08:05.474-06:00</current_datetime> layout plugin doesn't need to be covered. for both components and custom-components go through the utilities, declarations, etc. and add those audits where applicable.\n[tool bash -> success] args={\"command\":\"cd /Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken && grep -L \\\"pantoken-a11y-table\\\" docs/api/css/*.md | xargs -n1 basename; sed -n 1,60p formats/components/src/components/index.ts | head -60; cat formats/components/src/utilities/index.ts | head -40; ls formats/components/src/declarations plugins/pantoken/custom-components/src/declarations\",\"description\":\"List unaudited pages and source buckets\"}\n[tool bash -> success] args={\"command\":\"cd /Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken && head -5 docs/api/css/color.md docs/api/css/primitives.md docs/api/css/base.md docs/api/css/breakpoints.md docs/api/css/maskglobal.md | cut -c1-200; cat formats/components/src/rules/index.ts | grep -v \\\"^ \\\\*\\\\|^/\\\\*\\\" ; cat formats/components/src/declarations/index.ts | grep -v \\\"^ \\\\*\\\\|^/\\\\*\\\"; cd formats/components/src; for f in utilities/*/*.css rules/*/*.css declarations/*/*.css; do echo \\\"$f a11y=$(grep -c '@a11y\\\\|@accessibility' $f) ex=$(grep -c '@example' $f) auto=$(grep -c automatica11y $f)\\\"; done\",\"description\":\"Survey records for a11y and examples\"}\n[tool bash -> success] args={\"command\":\"cd /Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components && cat > /tmp/survey.ts <<'E'\\nimport { parseCssDocs } from \\\"@cssdoc/core\\\";\\nimport { UTILITIES } from \\\"/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/utilities/index.ts\\\";\\nimport { RULES } from \\\"/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/rules/index.ts\\\";\\nimport { DECLARATIONS } from \\\"/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/declarations/index.ts\\\";\\nimport { resolveExampleTargets } from \\\"@pantoken/utils/example-targets\\\";\\nfor (const [k, list] of [[\\\"util\\\", UTILITIES], [\\\"rule\\\", RULES], [\\\"decl\\\", DECLARATIONS]] as const)\\n for (const r of list) {\\n const es = parseCssDocs(r.rules(\\\"instui-\\\")).filter((e) => e.name === r.name);\\n const e = es[0];\\n console.log(k, r.name, \\\"entries\\\", es.length, \\\"a11y\\\", !!e?.accessibility?.trim(), \\\"ex\\\", e?.examples.length, \\\"auto\\\", e ? resolveExampleTargets(e.examples).automatica11y.length : \\\"-\\\");\\n }\\nE\\ncp /tmp/survey.ts scripts/_survey.ts && node scripts/_survey.ts 2>&1 | tail -30; rm scripts/_survey.ts\",\"description\":\"Survey utility/rule/declaration records\"}\n[tool bash -> success] args={\"command\":\"cd /Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src && ls utilities/spacing utilities/transition utilities/truncate; sed -n 1,60p utilities/truncate/index.ts; sed -n 1,40p utilities/transition/transition.css; grep -n \\\"color\\\" ../scripts/generate.ts | head -20; sed -n 1,80p lib/define.ts | head -90\",\"description\":\"See how utility records are authored\"}\n[tool bash -> success] args={\"command\":\"cd /Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/utilities && sed -n 10,60p truncate/index.ts; echo ======; sed -n 1,40p transition/transition.css\",\"description\":\"Truncate and transition\"}\n[tool bash -> success] args={\"command\":\"cd /Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken && grep -rn \\\"@utility color\\\\|@component color\\\\|--text-danger\\\" --include=*.ts formats/components/src formats/components/scripts -l | head; sed -n 1,30p docs/api/css/color.md | cut -c1-300\",\"description\":\"Locate color record\"}\n[tool bash -> success] args={\"command\":\"cd /Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components && grep -n \\\"@utility color\\\" -B12 -A25 scripts/generate.ts | head -90\",\"description\":\"Color record in generate.ts\"}","copilot_cache_control":{"type":"ephemeral"}},{"content":"ALLOW: Adds accessibility guidance and an audit example to an in-scope utility source file.","refusal":null,"role":"assistant","reasoning_opaque":"REDACTED","reasoning_text":"**Evaluating accessibility guidelines**\n\nI need to assess the proposed edits. The user asked about broad work utilities, and this task involves adding accessibility guidance to a source document. I’m checking if an audit for examples could be run, even though it’s inert documentation. It’s important to ensure any edits meet requirements and don’t cause issues. The user’s request is to add audits where necessary, so I need to keep the edits within a specific scope without causing disruptions.","encrypted_content":"REDACTED","reasoningBlocks":{"provider":"openai-responses","blocks":[{"content":[],"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"","summary":[{"text":"**Evaluating accessibility guidelines**\n\nI need to assess the proposed edits. The user asked about broad work utilities, and this task involves adding accessibility guidance to a source document. I’m checking if an audit for examples could be run, even though it’s inert documentation. It’s important to ensure any edits meet requirements and don’t cause issues. The user’s request is to add audits where necessary, so I need to keep the edits within a specific scope without causing disruptions.","type":"summary_text"}],"type":"reasoning"}]},"responses_message_status":"completed","phase":"final_answer","serverTools":{"provider":"openai-responses"},"apiCallId":"","outputTokens":163,"providerId":"copilot"}]},"id":"cfb0e948-5e04-44d4-9d4a-a80d0f428207","timestamp":"2026-10-28T19:10:18.676Z","parentId":"417d5108-c9a4-44d4-92e2-7edc1e302cd4"}
{"type":"permission.requested","data":{"requestId":"869e446e-c598-489f-946a-ca85b6f63d9b","permissionRequest":{"kind":"write","toolCallId":"toolu_01KdmPT9UdhrmxqVzvJ2MtR3","intention":"Edit file","fileName":"/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/utilities/responsive/index.ts","diff":"\ndiff --git a/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/utilities/responsive/index.ts b/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/utilities/responsive/index.ts\nindex 0000000..0000000 100644\n--- a/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/utilities/responsive/index.ts\n+++ b/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/utilities/responsive/index.ts\n@@ -180,6 +180,12 @@\n  * @global\n  * @summary Viewport- or container-width show/hide classes across a themed breakpoint scale.\n  * @remarks \\`.instui-hidden-max-<bp>\\`/\\`-hidden-min-<bp>\\` hide by viewport width; \\`.instui-show-max-<bp>\\`/\\`-show-min-<bp>\\` are the inverse (hidden by default, shown only inside the range via \\`display: revert\\`); the \\`-cq-\\` variants react to a \\`.instui-container\\` ancestor's width instead, not the viewport's. Scale tiers \\`sm\\`/\\`md\\`/\\`lg\\`/\\`xl\\` mirror the IR's canonical breakpoint tokens, with a Pantoken-defined \\`xs\\` extension at \\`20em\\`; each is aliased to a long-form spelling (\\`x-small\\`\\u2013\\`x-large\\`) and a device name (\\`mobile\\`/\\`phablet\\`/\\`tablet\\`/\\`laptop\\`/\\`desktop\\`) \\u2014 both deprecated in favor of the short name \\u2014 plus the unscaled, themed \\`content\\`/\\`content-full-width\\` tiers (the main content area's max-width).\n+ * @a11y Hiding content at a breakpoint also hides it from assistive tech, so don't hide the only way to complete a task, and keep the shown and hidden versions equivalent in meaning.\n+ * @example -automatica11y\n+ * \\`\\`\\`html\n+ * <p class=\"instui-hidden-max-sm\">The full course description appears on larger screens.</p>\n+ * <p class=\"instui-show-min-sm\">The full course description appears on larger screens.</p>\n+ * \\`\\`\\`\n  * @example\n  * <div class=\"instui-hidden-max-sm\">Hidden at or below the small breakpoint.</div>\n  * <div class=\"instui-show-min-sm\">Shown only at or above the small breakpoint.</div>\n","newFileContents":"/**\n * The responsive-visibility utilities — the closest pure-CSS analogue to InstUI's `<Responsive>`:\n * viewport-width hide classes plus `-cq-` container-query variants.\n *\n * Not dual-chained onto every real component (unlike spacing/gap/layout): the alias post-processors\n * (`withSizeAliases`/`deprecatedAliasPairs` in `lib/aliases.ts`) scan this record's CSS body with\n * unanchored regexes, and this utility's selector lists (breakpoint × infix × short/long/device name)\n * are already large enough that adding ~70 more chained selectors per rule (one per real component)\n * pushes the scan into unusable-slow territory (confirmed: multi-minute hang during implementation).\n * Each rule does carry a bare `.-hidden-max-xs`-style dash modifier alongside the prefixed\n * `.instui-hidden-max-xs` class (a flat, constant-factor addition, not a per-component fan-out), so the\n * documented `@modifier` names resolve to a real selector.\n *\n * @module\n */\nimport { defineUtility, type Definition } from \"../../lib/define.ts\";\nimport { css } from \"../../lib/css.ts\";\nimport type { ComponentTheme } from \"../../lib/helpers.ts\";\nimport { breakpointEm } from \"../../lib/breakpoints.ts\";\n\n/** Short name, long-form spelling, and device name for each responsive breakpoint tier. */\nconst SCALE_TIERS: readonly [short: string, long: string, device: string][] = [\n  [\"xs\", \"x-small\", \"mobile\"],\n  [\"sm\", \"small\", \"phablet\"],\n  [\"md\", \"medium\", \"tablet\"],\n  [\"lg\", \"large\", \"laptop\"],\n  [\"xl\", \"x-large\", \"desktop\"],\n];\n\n/** Pantoken's extra-small extension, below InstUI's canonical `sm` breakpoint. */\nconst XS_BREAKPOINT_EM = \"20em\";\n\n/** `[names sharing one breakpoint value, width]` for the scale tiers — theme-invariant. */\nconst scaleBreakpoints = (): [string[], string][] =>\n  SCALE_TIERS.map(([short, long, device]) => [\n    [short, long, device],\n    short === \"xs\" ? XS_BREAKPOINT_EM : breakpointEm(`--instui-breakpoints-${short}`),\n  ]);\n\n/** The main content area's max-width, in em, per theme — hand-authored (not in the token IR). */\nconst CONTENT_BREAKPOINT_EM: Record<ComponentTheme, { content: string; contentFullWidth: string }> =\n  {\n    rebrand: { content: \"68.75em\", contentFullWidth: \"98.75em\" }, // 1100px / 1580px\n    canvas: { content: \"59.25em\", contentFullWidth: \"59.25em\" },\n    canvasHighContrast: { content: \"59.25em\", contentFullWidth: \"59.25em\" },\n  };\n\n/** The responsive-visibility utility — viewport-width hide classes plus `-cq-` container-query variants. */\nexport const responsive: Definition = defineUtility({\n  name: \"responsive\",\n  css: (p, options) => {\n    const theme = options?.theme ?? \"rebrand\";\n    const { content, contentFullWidth } = CONTENT_BREAKPOINT_EM[theme];\n    // Scale tiers get short + long-form + device-name twins; the named tiers below don't (no scale to twin against).\n    const bp: [string[], string][] = [\n      ...scaleBreakpoints(),\n      [[\"content\"], content],\n      [[\"content-full-width\"], contentFullWidth],\n    ];\n    const selectors = (prefix: string, infix: string, names: string[]): string =>\n      names.map((name) => `.${prefix}${infix}${name}, .-${infix}${name}`).join(\", \");\n    const viewport = bp\n      .map(\n        ([names, w]) =>\n          `@media (max-width: ${w}) { ${selectors(p, \"hidden-max-\", names)} { display: none !important; } }\\n` +\n          `@media (min-width: ${w}) { ${selectors(p, \"hidden-min-\", names)} { display: none !important; } }`,\n      )\n      .join(\"\\n\");\n    // Container-query variants — the true InstUI <Responsive> analogue: mark an ancestor `.<prefix>-container`\n    // and these react to ITS width, not the viewport's. Same breakpoint scale, `-cq-` infix.\n    const container = bp\n      .map(\n        ([names, w]) =>\n          `@container (max-width: ${w}) { ${selectors(p, \"cq-hidden-max-\", names)} { display: none !important; } }\\n` +\n          `@container (min-width: ${w}) { ${selectors(p, \"cq-hidden-min-\", names)} { display: none !important; } }`,\n      )\n      .join(\"\\n\");\n    // `-show-*` is the inverse of `-hidden-*`: hidden by default, `revert`ed back to its natural\n    // display only inside the matching range. `revert` (not `initial`/`unset`, which would force\n    // `inline`) restores whatever display an earlier-origin rule (UA stylesheet, or an author rule\n    // this utility doesn't override) would have set — the standard technique for a display-agnostic\n    // show utility, though it can't see a same-origin author rule's `display` if one exists.\n    const showSelector = (infix: string): string =>\n      bp.map(([names]) => selectors(p, infix, names)).join(\", \");\n    const showBase = [\"show-max-\", \"show-min-\", \"cq-show-max-\", \"cq-show-min-\"]\n      .map(showSelector)\n      .join(\", \");\n    const showViewport = bp\n      .map(\n        ([names, w]) =>\n          `@media (max-width: ${w}) { ${selectors(p, \"show-max-\", names)} { display: revert !important; } }\\n` +\n          `@media (min-width: ${w}) { ${selectors(p, \"show-min-\", names)} { display: revert !important; } }`,\n      )\n      .join(\"\\n\");\n    const showContainer = bp\n      .map(\n        ([names, w]) =>\n          `@container (max-width: ${w}) { ${selectors(p, \"cq-show-max-\", names)} { display: revert !important; } }\\n` +\n          `@container (min-width: ${w}) { ${selectors(p, \"cq-show-min-\", names)} { display: revert !important; } }`,\n      )\n      .join(\"\\n\");\n    // The @media/@container queries only define a threshold — they don't hide anything themselves\n    // (the classes below do); describe the threshold, not the visibility behavior.\n    const conditionDocs = bp\n      .map(\n        ([names, w]) =>\n          ` * @media (max-width: ${w}) — Upper bound of the \\`${names[0]}\\` breakpoint.\\n` +\n          ` * @media (min-width: ${w}) — Lower bound of the \\`${names[0]}\\` breakpoint.\\n` +\n          ` * @container (max-width: ${w}) — Upper bound of the \\`${names[0]}\\` breakpoint, evaluated against a marked container.\\n` +\n          ` * @container (min-width: ${w}) — Lower bound of the \\`${names[0]}\\` breakpoint, evaluated against a marked container.`,\n      )\n      .join(\"\\n\");\n    // Every hide class, documented; long-form/device-name twins are `@alias` aliases of the short\n    // name (cssdoc renders these the same way as the size-scale's `-size-small`/`-size-sm` aliases).\n    const modifierDocs = bp\n      .map(([names, w]) => {\n        const [short, ...aliases] = names;\n        const canonical = [\n          ` * @modifier -hidden-max-${short} — Hide when the viewport is at or below the \\`${short}\\` breakpoint (\\`${w}\\`).`,\n          ` * @modifier -hidden-min-${short} — Hide when the viewport is at or above the \\`${short}\\` breakpoint (\\`${w}\\`).`,\n          ` * @modifier -cq-hidden-max-${short} — Hide when the marked container is at or below the \\`${short}\\` breakpoint (\\`${w}\\`).`,\n          ` * @modifier -cq-hidden-min-${short} — Hide when the marked container is at or above the \\`${short}\\` breakpoint (\\`${w}\\`).`,\n        ];\n        const aliasDocs = aliases.flatMap((alias) => [\n          ` * @modifier -hidden-max-${alias} — @alias {@link -hidden-max-${short}}`,\n          ` * @modifier -hidden-min-${alias} — @alias {@link -hidden-min-${short}}`,\n          ` * @modifier -cq-hidden-max-${alias} — @alias {@link -cq-hidden-max-${short}}`,\n          ` * @modifier -cq-hidden-min-${alias} — @alias {@link -cq-hidden-min-${short}}`,\n        ]);\n        const showCanonical = [\n          ` * @modifier -show-max-${short} — Show (inverse of \\`-hidden-min-${short}\\`) when the viewport is at or below the \\`${short}\\` breakpoint (\\`${w}\\`); hidden otherwise.`,\n          ` * @modifier -show-min-${short} — Show (inverse of \\`-hidden-max-${short}\\`) when the viewport is at or above the \\`${short}\\` breakpoint (\\`${w}\\`); hidden otherwise.`,\n          ` * @modifier -cq-show-max-${short} — Show when the marked container is at or below the \\`${short}\\` breakpoint (\\`${w}\\`); hidden otherwise.`,\n          ` * @modifier -cq-show-min-${short} — Show when the marked container is at or above the \\`${short}\\` breakpoint (\\`${w}\\`); hidden otherwise.`,\n        ];\n        const showAliasDocs = aliases.flatMap((alias) => [\n          ` * @modifier -show-max-${alias} — @alias {@link -show-max-${short}}`,\n          ` * @modifier -show-min-${alias} — @alias {@link -show-min-${short}}`,\n          ` * @modifier -cq-show-max-${alias} — @alias {@link -cq-show-max-${short}}`,\n          ` * @modifier -cq-show-min-${alias} — @alias {@link -cq-show-min-${short}}`,\n        ]);\n        return [...canonical, ...aliasDocs, ...showCanonical, ...showAliasDocs].join(\"\\n\");\n      })\n      .join(\"\\n\");\n    // `@property` registers each breakpoint as an inspectable custom property (informational only —\n    // changing it does NOT move the compiled `@media`/`@container` thresholds above, since browsers\n    // can't read a custom property back into a media feature). `initial-value` must be a literal (CSS\n    // rejects `var()` there), so the scale tiers' real value is wired separately below, via `var(...)`\n    // on the same property — that's what makes `--instui-component-tray-width-*` show as consumed.\n    const properties = bp\n      .map(\n        ([names, w]) =>\n          `@property --pantoken-bp-${names[0]} { syntax: \"<length>\"; inherits: true; initial-value: ${w}; }`,\n      )\n      .join(\"\\n\");\n    const scaleSourceVars = SCALE_TIERS.map(([short]) =>\n      short === \"xs\"\n        ? `  --pantoken-bp-xs: ${XS_BREAKPOINT_EM};`\n        : `  --pantoken-bp-${short}: var(--instui-breakpoints-${short});`,\n    ).join(\"\\n\");\n    const canonicalScaleNames = new Set(SCALE_TIERS.slice(1).map(([short]) => short));\n    // Each `@property` gets real prose: scale tiers name the IR token they mirror; the two\n    // unscaled, themed tiers say so instead, since they aren't backed by a token.\n    const propertyDocs = bp\n      .map(([names, w]) => {\n        const short = names[0];\n        const source = canonicalScaleNames.has(short)\n          ? `mirrors \\`--instui-breakpoints-${short}\\``\n          : short === \"xs\"\n            ? \"hand-authored Pantoken extension (not in the token IR)\"\n            : \"hand-authored, themed (not in the token IR)\";\n        return ` * @cssproperty --pantoken-bp-${short} <length> — The \\`${short}\\` breakpoint's value (\\`${w}\\`, ${source}). Overriding it does not move the compiled \\`@media\\`/\\`@container\\` thresholds above.`;\n      })\n      .join(\"\\n\");\n    // prettier-ignore\n    return css`\n/**\n * @utility responsive\n * @selector [class*=\"-hidden-\"],[class*=\"-show-\"]\n * @global\n * @summary Viewport- or container-width show/hide classes across a themed breakpoint scale.\n * @remarks \\`.instui-hidden-max-<bp>\\`/\\`-hidden-min-<bp>\\` hide by viewport width; \\`.instui-show-max-<bp>\\`/\\`-show-min-<bp>\\` are the inverse (hidden by default, shown only inside the range via \\`display: revert\\`); the \\`-cq-\\` variants react to a \\`.instui-container\\` ancestor's width instead, not the viewport's. Scale tiers \\`sm\\`/\\`md\\`/\\`lg\\`/\\`xl\\` mirror the IR's canonical breakpoint tokens, with a Pantoken-defined \\`xs\\` extension at \\`20em\\`; each is aliased to a long-form spelling (\\`x-small\\`\\u2013\\`x-large\\`) and a device name (\\`mobile\\`/\\`phablet\\`/\\`tablet\\`/\\`laptop\\`/\\`desktop\\`) \\u2014 both deprecated in favor of the short name \\u2014 plus the unscaled, themed \\`content\\`/\\`content-full-width\\` tiers (the main content area's max-width).\n * @a11y Hiding content at a breakpoint also hides it from assistive tech, so don't hide the only way to complete a task, and keep the shown and hidden versions equivalent in meaning.\n * @example -automatica11y\n * \\`\\`\\`html\n * <p class=\"instui-hidden-max-sm\">The full course description appears on larger screens.</p>\n * <p class=\"instui-show-min-sm\">The full course description appears on larger screens.</p>\n * \\`\\`\\`\n * @example\n * <div class=\"instui-hidden-max-sm\">Hidden at or below the small breakpoint.</div>\n * <div class=\"instui-show-min-sm\">Shown only at or above the small breakpoint.</div>\n${modifierDocs}\n${conditionDocs}\n${propertyDocs}\n */\n${properties}\n:root {\n${scaleSourceVars}\n}\n${viewport}\n.${p}container { container-type: inline-size; }\n${container}\n${showBase} { display: none !important; }\n${showViewport}\n${showContainer}\n`;\n  },\n});\n\n/** The responsive-visibility utilities as a standalone, header-wrapped stylesheet. */\nexport const responsiveUtilitiesCss: Definition[\"css\"] = responsive.css;\n","canOfferSessionApproval":true,"fileEdits":[{"before":{"path":"/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/utilities/responsive/index.ts","content":"/**\n * The responsive-visibility utilities — the closest pure-CSS analogue to InstUI's `<Responsive>`:\n * viewport-width hide classes plus `-cq-` container-query variants.\n *\n * Not dual-chained onto every real component (unlike spacing/gap/layout): the alias post-processors\n * (`withSizeAliases`/`deprecatedAliasPairs` in `lib/aliases.ts`) scan this record's CSS body with\n * unanchored regexes, and this utility's selector lists (breakpoint × infix × short/long/device name)\n * are already large enough that adding ~70 more chained selectors per rule (one per real component)\n * pushes the scan into unusable-slow territory (confirmed: multi-minute hang during implementation).\n * Each rule does carry a bare `.-hidden-max-xs`-style dash modifier alongside the prefixed\n * `.instui-hidden-max-xs` class (a flat, constant-factor addition, not a per-component fan-out), so the\n * documented `@modifier` names resolve to a real selector.\n *\n * @module\n */\nimport { defineUtility, type Definition } from \"../../lib/define.ts\";\nimport { css } from \"../../lib/css.ts\";\nimport type { ComponentTheme } from \"../../lib/helpers.ts\";\nimport { breakpointEm } from \"../../lib/breakpoints.ts\";\n\n/** Short name, long-form spelling, and device name for each responsive breakpoint tier. */\nconst SCALE_TIERS: readonly [short: string, long: string, device: string][] = [\n  [\"xs\", \"x-small\", \"mobile\"],\n  [\"sm\", \"small\", \"phablet\"],\n  [\"md\", \"medium\", \"tablet\"],\n  [\"lg\", \"large\", \"laptop\"],\n  [\"xl\", \"x-large\", \"desktop\"],\n];\n\n/** Pantoken's extra-small extension, below InstUI's canonical `sm` breakpoint. */\nconst XS_BREAKPOINT_EM = \"20em\";\n\n/** `[names sharing one breakpoint value, width]` for the scale tiers — theme-invariant. */\nconst scaleBreakpoints = (): [string[], string][] =>\n  SCALE_TIERS.map(([short, long, device]) => [\n    [short, long, device],\n    short === \"xs\" ? XS_BREAKPOINT_EM : breakpointEm(`--instui-breakpoints-${short}`),\n  ]);\n\n/** The main content area's max-width, in em, per theme — hand-authored (not in the token IR). */\nconst CONTENT_BREAKPOINT_EM: Record<ComponentTheme, { content: string; contentFullWidth: string }> =\n  {\n    rebrand: { content: \"68.75em\", contentFullWidth: \"98.75em\" }, // 1100px / 1580px\n    canvas: { content: \"59.25em\", contentFullWidth: \"59.25em\" },\n    canvasHighContrast: { content: \"59.25em\", contentFullWidth: \"59.25em\" },\n  };\n\n/** The responsive-visibility utility — viewport-width hide classes plus `-cq-` container-query variants. */\nexport const responsive: Definition = defineUtility({\n  name: \"responsive\",\n  css: (p, options) => {\n    const theme = options?.theme ?? \"rebrand\";\n    const { content, contentFullWidth } = CONTENT_BREAKPOINT_EM[theme];\n    // Scale tiers get short + long-form + device-name twins; the named tiers below don't (no scale to twin against).\n    const bp: [string[], string][] = [\n      ...scaleBreakpoints(),\n      [[\"content\"], content],\n      [[\"content-full-width\"], contentFullWidth],\n    ];\n    const selectors = (prefix: string, infix: string, names: string[]): string =>\n      names.map((name) => `.${prefix}${infix}${name}, .-${infix}${name}`).join(\", \");\n    const viewport = bp\n      .map(\n        ([names, w]) =>\n          `@media (max-width: ${w}) { ${selectors(p, \"hidden-max-\", names)} { display: none !important; } }\\n` +\n          `@media (min-width: ${w}) { ${selectors(p, \"hidden-min-\", names)} { display: none !important; } }`,\n      )\n      .join(\"\\n\");\n    // Container-query variants — the true InstUI <Responsive> analogue: mark an ancestor `.<prefix>-container`\n    // and these react to ITS width, not the viewport's. Same breakpoint scale, `-cq-` infix.\n    const container = bp\n      .map(\n        ([names, w]) =>\n          `@container (max-width: ${w}) { ${selectors(p, \"cq-hidden-max-\", names)} { display: none !important; } }\\n` +\n          `@container (min-width: ${w}) { ${selectors(p, \"cq-hidden-min-\", names)} { display: none !important; } }`,\n      )\n      .join(\"\\n\");\n    // `-show-*` is the inverse of `-hidden-*`: hidden by default, `revert`ed back to its natural\n    // display only inside the matching range. `revert` (not `initial`/`unset`, which would force\n    // `inline`) restores whatever display an earlier-origin rule (UA stylesheet, or an author rule\n    // this utility doesn't override) would have set — the standard technique for a display-agnostic\n    // show utility, though it can't see a same-origin author rule's `display` if one exists.\n    const showSelector = (infix: string): string =>\n      bp.map(([names]) => selectors(p, infix, names)).join(\", \");\n    const showBase = [\"show-max-\", \"show-min-\", \"cq-show-max-\", \"cq-show-min-\"]\n      .map(showSelector)\n      .join(\", \");\n    const showViewport = bp\n      .map(\n        ([names, w]) =>\n          `@media (max-width: ${w}) { ${selectors(p, \"show-max-\", names)} { display: revert !important; } }\\n` +\n          `@media (min-width: ${w}) { ${selectors(p, \"show-min-\", names)} { display: revert !important; } }`,\n      )\n      .join(\"\\n\");\n    const showContainer = bp\n      .map(\n        ([names, w]) =>\n          `@container (max-width: ${w}) { ${selectors(p, \"cq-show-max-\", names)} { display: revert !important; } }\\n` +\n          `@container (min-width: ${w}) { ${selectors(p, \"cq-show-min-\", names)} { display: revert !important; } }`,\n      )\n      .join(\"\\n\");\n    // The @media/@container queries only define a threshold — they don't hide anything themselves\n    // (the classes below do); describe the threshold, not the visibility behavior.\n    const conditionDocs = bp\n      .map(\n        ([names, w]) =>\n          ` * @media (max-width: ${w}) — Upper bound of the \\`${names[0]}\\` breakpoint.\\n` +\n          ` * @media (min-width: ${w}) — Lower bound of the \\`${names[0]}\\` breakpoint.\\n` +\n          ` * @container (max-width: ${w}) — Upper bound of the \\`${names[0]}\\` breakpoint, evaluated against a marked container.\\n` +\n          ` * @container (min-width: ${w}) — Lower bound of the \\`${names[0]}\\` breakpoint, evaluated against a marked container.`,\n      )\n      .join(\"\\n\");\n    // Every hide class, documented; long-form/device-name twins are `@alias` aliases of the short\n    // name (cssdoc renders these the same way as the size-scale's `-size-small`/`-size-sm` aliases).\n    const modifierDocs = bp\n      .map(([names, w]) => {\n        const [short, ...aliases] = names;\n        const canonical = [\n          ` * @modifier -hidden-max-${short} — Hide when the viewport is at or below the \\`${short}\\` breakpoint (\\`${w}\\`).`,\n          ` * @modifier -hidden-min-${short} — Hide when the viewport is at or above the \\`${short}\\` breakpoint (\\`${w}\\`).`,\n          ` * @modifier -cq-hidden-max-${short} — Hide when the marked container is at or below the \\`${short}\\` breakpoint (\\`${w}\\`).`,\n          ` * @modifier -cq-hidden-min-${short} — Hide when the marked container is at or above the \\`${short}\\` breakpoint (\\`${w}\\`).`,\n        ];\n        const aliasDocs = aliases.flatMap((alias) => [\n          ` * @modifier -hidden-max-${alias} — @alias {@link -hidden-max-${short}}`,\n          ` * @modifier -hidden-min-${alias} — @alias {@link -hidden-min-${short}}`,\n          ` * @modifier -cq-hidden-max-${alias} — @alias {@link -cq-hidden-max-${short}}`,\n          ` * @modifier -cq-hidden-min-${alias} — @alias {@link -cq-hidden-min-${short}}`,\n        ]);\n        const showCanonical = [\n          ` * @modifier -show-max-${short} — Show (inverse of \\`-hidden-min-${short}\\`) when the viewport is at or below the \\`${short}\\` breakpoint (\\`${w}\\`); hidden otherwise.`,\n          ` * @modifier -show-min-${short} — Show (inverse of \\`-hidden-max-${short}\\`) when the viewport is at or above the \\`${short}\\` breakpoint (\\`${w}\\`); hidden otherwise.`,\n          ` * @modifier -cq-show-max-${short} — Show when the marked container is at or below the \\`${short}\\` breakpoint (\\`${w}\\`); hidden otherwise.`,\n          ` * @modifier -cq-show-min-${short} — Show when the marked container is at or above the \\`${short}\\` breakpoint (\\`${w}\\`); hidden otherwise.`,\n        ];\n        const showAliasDocs = aliases.flatMap((alias) => [\n          ` * @modifier -show-max-${alias} — @alias {@link -show-max-${short}}`,\n          ` * @modifier -show-min-${alias} — @alias {@link -show-min-${short}}`,\n          ` * @modifier -cq-show-max-${alias} — @alias {@link -cq-show-max-${short}}`,\n          ` * @modifier -cq-show-min-${alias} — @alias {@link -cq-show-min-${short}}`,\n        ]);\n        return [...canonical, ...aliasDocs, ...showCanonical, ...showAliasDocs].join(\"\\n\");\n      })\n      .join(\"\\n\");\n    // `@property` registers each breakpoint as an inspectable custom property (informational only —\n    // changing it does NOT move the compiled `@media`/`@container` thresholds above, since browsers\n    // can't read a custom property back into a media feature). `initial-value` must be a literal (CSS\n    // rejects `var()` there), so the scale tiers' real value is wired separately below, via `var(...)`\n    // on the same property — that's what makes `--instui-component-tray-width-*` show as consumed.\n    const properties = bp\n      .map(\n        ([names, w]) =>\n          `@property --pantoken-bp-${names[0]} { syntax: \"<length>\"; inherits: true; initial-value: ${w}; }`,\n      )\n      .join(\"\\n\");\n    const scaleSourceVars = SCALE_TIERS.map(([short]) =>\n      short === \"xs\"\n        ? `  --pantoken-bp-xs: ${XS_BREAKPOINT_EM};`\n        : `  --pantoken-bp-${short}: var(--instui-breakpoints-${short});`,\n    ).join(\"\\n\");\n    const canonicalScaleNames = new Set(SCALE_TIERS.slice(1).map(([short]) => short));\n    // Each `@property` gets real prose: scale tiers name the IR token they mirror; the two\n    // unscaled, themed tiers say so instead, since they aren't backed by a token.\n    const propertyDocs = bp\n      .map(([names, w]) => {\n        const short = names[0];\n        const source = canonicalScaleNames.has(short)\n          ? `mirrors \\`--instui-breakpoints-${short}\\``\n          : short === \"xs\"\n            ? \"hand-authored Pantoken extension (not in the token IR)\"\n            : \"hand-authored, themed (not in the token IR)\";\n        return ` * @cssproperty --pantoken-bp-${short} <length> — The \\`${short}\\` breakpoint's value (\\`${w}\\`, ${source}). Overriding it does not move the compiled \\`@media\\`/\\`@container\\` thresholds above.`;\n      })\n      .join(\"\\n\");\n    // prettier-ignore\n    return css`\n/**\n * @utility responsive\n * @selector [class*=\"-hidden-\"],[class*=\"-show-\"]\n * @global\n * @summary Viewport- or container-width show/hide classes across a themed breakpoint scale.\n * @remarks \\`.instui-hidden-max-<bp>\\`/\\`-hidden-min-<bp>\\` hide by viewport width; \\`.instui-show-max-<bp>\\`/\\`-show-min-<bp>\\` are the inverse (hidden by default, shown only inside the range via \\`display: revert\\`); the \\`-cq-\\` variants react to a \\`.instui-container\\` ancestor's width instead, not the viewport's. Scale tiers \\`sm\\`/\\`md\\`/\\`lg\\`/\\`xl\\` mirror the IR's canonical breakpoint tokens, with a Pantoken-defined \\`xs\\` extension at \\`20em\\`; each is aliased to a long-form spelling (\\`x-small\\`\\u2013\\`x-large\\`) and a device name (\\`mobile\\`/\\`phablet\\`/\\`tablet\\`/\\`laptop\\`/\\`desktop\\`) \\u2014 both deprecated in favor of the short name \\u2014 plus the unscaled, themed \\`content\\`/\\`content-full-width\\` tiers (the main content area's max-width).\n * @example\n * <div class=\"instui-hidden-max-sm\">Hidden at or below the small breakpoint.</div>\n * <div class=\"instui-show-min-sm\">Shown only at or above the small breakpoint.</div>\n${modifierDocs}\n${conditionDocs}\n${propertyDocs}\n */\n${properties}\n:root {\n${scaleSourceVars}\n}\n${viewport}\n.${p}container { container-type: inline-size; }\n${container}\n${showBase} { display: none !important; }\n${showViewport}\n${showContainer}\n`;\n  },\n});\n\n/** The responsive-visibility utilities as a standalone, header-wrapped stylesheet. */\nexport const responsiveUtilitiesCss: Definition[\"css\"] = responsive.css;\n"},"after":{"path":"/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/utilities/responsive/index.ts","content":"/**\n * The responsive-visibility utilities — the closest pure-CSS analogue to InstUI's `<Responsive>`:\n * viewport-width hide classes plus `-cq-` container-query variants.\n *\n * Not dual-chained onto every real component (unlike spacing/gap/layout): the alias post-processors\n * (`withSizeAliases`/`deprecatedAliasPairs` in `lib/aliases.ts`) scan this record's CSS body with\n * unanchored regexes, and this utility's selector lists (breakpoint × infix × short/long/device name)\n * are already large enough that adding ~70 more chained selectors per rule (one per real component)\n * pushes the scan into unusable-slow territory (confirmed: multi-minute hang during implementation).\n * Each rule does carry a bare `.-hidden-max-xs`-style dash modifier alongside the prefixed\n * `.instui-hidden-max-xs` class (a flat, constant-factor addition, not a per-component fan-out), so the\n * documented `@modifier` names resolve to a real selector.\n *\n * @module\n */\nimport { defineUtility, type Definition } from \"../../lib/define.ts\";\nimport { css } from \"../../lib/css.ts\";\nimport type { ComponentTheme } from \"../../lib/helpers.ts\";\nimport { breakpointEm } from \"../../lib/breakpoints.ts\";\n\n/** Short name, long-form spelling, and device name for each responsive breakpoint tier. */\nconst SCALE_TIERS: readonly [short: string, long: string, device: string][] = [\n  [\"xs\", \"x-small\", \"mobile\"],\n  [\"sm\", \"small\", \"phablet\"],\n  [\"md\", \"medium\", \"tablet\"],\n  [\"lg\", \"large\", \"laptop\"],\n  [\"xl\", \"x-large\", \"desktop\"],\n];\n\n/** Pantoken's extra-small extension, below InstUI's canonical `sm` breakpoint. */\nconst XS_BREAKPOINT_EM = \"20em\";\n\n/** `[names sharing one breakpoint value, width]` for the scale tiers — theme-invariant. */\nconst scaleBreakpoints = (): [string[], string][] =>\n  SCALE_TIERS.map(([short, long, device]) => [\n    [short, long, device],\n    short === \"xs\" ? XS_BREAKPOINT_EM : breakpointEm(`--instui-breakpoints-${short}`),\n  ]);\n\n/** The main content area's max-width, in em, per theme — hand-authored (not in the token IR). */\nconst CONTENT_BREAKPOINT_EM: Record<ComponentTheme, { content: string; contentFullWidth: string }> =\n  {\n    rebrand: { content: \"68.75em\", contentFullWidth: \"98.75em\" }, // 1100px / 1580px\n    canvas: { content: \"59.25em\", contentFullWidth: \"59.25em\" },\n    canvasHighContrast: { content: \"59.25em\", contentFullWidth: \"59.25em\" },\n  };\n\n/** The responsive-visibility utility — viewport-width hide classes plus `-cq-` container-query variants. */\nexport const responsive: Definition = defineUtility({\n  name: \"responsive\",\n  css: (p, options) => {\n    const theme = options?.theme ?? \"rebrand\";\n    const { content, contentFullWidth } = CONTENT_BREAKPOINT_EM[theme];\n    // Scale tiers get short + long-form + device-name twins; the named tiers below don't (no scale to twin against).\n    const bp: [string[], string][] = [\n      ...scaleBreakpoints(),\n      [[\"content\"], content],\n      [[\"content-full-width\"], contentFullWidth],\n    ];\n    const selectors = (prefix: string, infix: string, names: string[]): string =>\n      names.map((name) => `.${prefix}${infix}${name}, .-${infix}${name}`).join(\", \");\n    const viewport = bp\n      .map(\n        ([names, w]) =>\n          `@media (max-width: ${w}) { ${selectors(p, \"hidden-max-\", names)} { display: none !important; } }\\n` +\n          `@media (min-width: ${w}) { ${selectors(p, \"hidden-min-\", names)} { display: none !important; } }`,\n      )\n      .join(\"\\n\");\n    // Container-query variants — the true InstUI <Responsive> analogue: mark an ancestor `.<prefix>-container`\n    // and these react to ITS width, not the viewport's. Same breakpoint scale, `-cq-` infix.\n    const container = bp\n      .map(\n        ([names, w]) =>\n          `@container (max-width: ${w}) { ${selectors(p, \"cq-hidden-max-\", names)} { display: none !important; } }\\n` +\n          `@container (min-width: ${w}) { ${selectors(p, \"cq-hidden-min-\", names)} { display: none !important; } }`,\n      )\n      .join(\"\\n\");\n    // `-show-*` is the inverse of `-hidden-*`: hidden by default, `revert`ed back to its natural\n    // display only inside the matching range. `revert` (not `initial`/`unset`, which would force\n    // `inline`) restores whatever display an earlier-origin rule (UA stylesheet, or an author rule\n    // this utility doesn't override) would have set — the standard technique for a display-agnostic\n    // show utility, though it can't see a same-origin author rule's `display` if one exists.\n    const showSelector = (infix: string): string =>\n      bp.map(([names]) => selectors(p, infix, names)).join(\", \");\n    const showBase = [\"show-max-\", \"show-min-\", \"cq-show-max-\", \"cq-show-min-\"]\n      .map(showSelector)\n      .join(\", \");\n    const showViewport = bp\n      .map(\n        ([names, w]) =>\n          `@media (max-width: ${w}) { ${selectors(p, \"show-max-\", names)} { display: revert !important; } }\\n` +\n          `@media (min-width: ${w}) { ${selectors(p, \"show-min-\", names)} { display: revert !important; } }`,\n      )\n      .join(\"\\n\");\n    const showContainer = bp\n      .map(\n        ([names, w]) =>\n          `@container (max-width: ${w}) { ${selectors(p, \"cq-show-max-\", names)} { display: revert !important; } }\\n` +\n          `@container (min-width: ${w}) { ${selectors(p, \"cq-show-min-\", names)} { display: revert !important; } }`,\n      )\n      .join(\"\\n\");\n    // The @media/@container queries only define a threshold — they don't hide anything themselves\n    // (the classes below do); describe the threshold, not the visibility behavior.\n    const conditionDocs = bp\n      .map(\n        ([names, w]) =>\n          ` * @media (max-width: ${w}) — Upper bound of the \\`${names[0]}\\` breakpoint.\\n` +\n          ` * @media (min-width: ${w}) — Lower bound of the \\`${names[0]}\\` breakpoint.\\n` +\n          ` * @container (max-width: ${w}) — Upper bound of the \\`${names[0]}\\` breakpoint, evaluated against a marked container.\\n` +\n          ` * @container (min-width: ${w}) — Lower bound of the \\`${names[0]}\\` breakpoint, evaluated against a marked container.`,\n      )\n      .join(\"\\n\");\n    // Every hide class, documented; long-form/device-name twins are `@alias` aliases of the short\n    // name (cssdoc renders these the same way as the size-scale's `-size-small`/`-size-sm` aliases).\n    const modifierDocs = bp\n      .map(([names, w]) => {\n        const [short, ...aliases] = names;\n        const canonical = [\n          ` * @modifier -hidden-max-${short} — Hide when the viewport is at or below the \\`${short}\\` breakpoint (\\`${w}\\`).`,\n          ` * @modifier -hidden-min-${short} — Hide when the viewport is at or above the \\`${short}\\` breakpoint (\\`${w}\\`).`,\n          ` * @modifier -cq-hidden-max-${short} — Hide when the marked container is at or below the \\`${short}\\` breakpoint (\\`${w}\\`).`,\n          ` * @modifier -cq-hidden-min-${short} — Hide when the marked container is at or above the \\`${short}\\` breakpoint (\\`${w}\\`).`,\n        ];\n        const aliasDocs = aliases.flatMap((alias) => [\n          ` * @modifier -hidden-max-${alias} — @alias {@link -hidden-max-${short}}`,\n          ` * @modifier -hidden-min-${alias} — @alias {@link -hidden-min-${short}}`,\n          ` * @modifier -cq-hidden-max-${alias} — @alias {@link -cq-hidden-max-${short}}`,\n          ` * @modifier -cq-hidden-min-${alias} — @alias {@link -cq-hidden-min-${short}}`,\n        ]);\n        const showCanonical = [\n          ` * @modifier -show-max-${short} — Show (inverse of \\`-hidden-min-${short}\\`) when the viewport is at or below the \\`${short}\\` breakpoint (\\`${w}\\`); hidden otherwise.`,\n          ` * @modifier -show-min-${short} — Show (inverse of \\`-hidden-max-${short}\\`) when the viewport is at or above the \\`${short}\\` breakpoint (\\`${w}\\`); hidden otherwise.`,\n          ` * @modifier -cq-show-max-${short} — Show when the marked container is at or below the \\`${short}\\` breakpoint (\\`${w}\\`); hidden otherwise.`,\n          ` * @modifier -cq-show-min-${short} — Show when the marked container is at or above the \\`${short}\\` breakpoint (\\`${w}\\`); hidden otherwise.`,\n        ];\n        const showAliasDocs = aliases.flatMap((alias) => [\n          ` * @modifier -show-max-${alias} — @alias {@link -show-max-${short}}`,\n          ` * @modifier -show-min-${alias} — @alias {@link -show-min-${short}}`,\n          ` * @modifier -cq-show-max-${alias} — @alias {@link -cq-show-max-${short}}`,\n          ` * @modifier -cq-show-min-${alias} — @alias {@link -cq-show-min-${short}}`,\n        ]);\n        return [...canonical, ...aliasDocs, ...showCanonical, ...showAliasDocs].join(\"\\n\");\n      })\n      .join(\"\\n\");\n    // `@property` registers each breakpoint as an inspectable custom property (informational only —\n    // changing it does NOT move the compiled `@media`/`@container` thresholds above, since browsers\n    // can't read a custom property back into a media feature). `initial-value` must be a literal (CSS\n    // rejects `var()` there), so the scale tiers' real value is wired separately below, via `var(...)`\n    // on the same property — that's what makes `--instui-component-tray-width-*` show as consumed.\n    const properties = bp\n      .map(\n        ([names, w]) =>\n          `@property --pantoken-bp-${names[0]} { syntax: \"<length>\"; inherits: true; initial-value: ${w}; }`,\n      )\n      .join(\"\\n\");\n    const scaleSourceVars = SCALE_TIERS.map(([short]) =>\n      short === \"xs\"\n        ? `  --pantoken-bp-xs: ${XS_BREAKPOINT_EM};`\n        : `  --pantoken-bp-${short}: var(--instui-breakpoints-${short});`,\n    ).join(\"\\n\");\n    const canonicalScaleNames = new Set(SCALE_TIERS.slice(1).map(([short]) => short));\n    // Each `@property` gets real prose: scale tiers name the IR token they mirror; the two\n    // unscaled, themed tiers say so instead, since they aren't backed by a token.\n    const propertyDocs = bp\n      .map(([names, w]) => {\n        const short = names[0];\n        const source = canonicalScaleNames.has(short)\n          ? `mirrors \\`--instui-breakpoints-${short}\\``\n          : short === \"xs\"\n            ? \"hand-authored Pantoken extension (not in the token IR)\"\n            : \"hand-authored, themed (not in the token IR)\";\n        return ` * @cssproperty --pantoken-bp-${short} <length> — The \\`${short}\\` breakpoint's value (\\`${w}\\`, ${source}). Overriding it does not move the compiled \\`@media\\`/\\`@container\\` thresholds above.`;\n      })\n      .join(\"\\n\");\n    // prettier-ignore\n    return css`\n/**\n * @utility responsive\n * @selector [class*=\"-hidden-\"],[class*=\"-show-\"]\n * @global\n * @summary Viewport- or container-width show/hide classes across a themed breakpoint scale.\n * @remarks \\`.instui-hidden-max-<bp>\\`/\\`-hidden-min-<bp>\\` hide by viewport width; \\`.instui-show-max-<bp>\\`/\\`-show-min-<bp>\\` are the inverse (hidden by default, shown only inside the range via \\`display: revert\\`); the \\`-cq-\\` variants react to a \\`.instui-container\\` ancestor's width instead, not the viewport's. Scale tiers \\`sm\\`/\\`md\\`/\\`lg\\`/\\`xl\\` mirror the IR's canonical breakpoint tokens, with a Pantoken-defined \\`xs\\` extension at \\`20em\\`; each is aliased to a long-form spelling (\\`x-small\\`\\u2013\\`x-large\\`) and a device name (\\`mobile\\`/\\`phablet\\`/\\`tablet\\`/\\`laptop\\`/\\`desktop\\`) \\u2014 both deprecated in favor of the short name \\u2014 plus the unscaled, themed \\`content\\`/\\`content-full-width\\` tiers (the main content area's max-width).\n * @a11y Hiding content at a breakpoint also hides it from assistive tech, so don't hide the only way to complete a task, and keep the shown and hidden versions equivalent in meaning.\n * @example -automatica11y\n * \\`\\`\\`html\n * <p class=\"instui-hidden-max-sm\">The full course description appears on larger screens.</p>\n * <p class=\"instui-show-min-sm\">The full course description appears on larger screens.</p>\n * \\`\\`\\`\n * @example\n * <div class=\"instui-hidden-max-sm\">Hidden at or below the small breakpoint.</div>\n * <div class=\"instui-show-min-sm\">Shown only at or above the small breakpoint.</div>\n${modifierDocs}\n${conditionDocs}\n${propertyDocs}\n */\n${properties}\n:root {\n${scaleSourceVars}\n}\n${viewport}\n.${p}container { container-type: inline-size; }\n${container}\n${showBase} { display: none !important; }\n${showViewport}\n${showContainer}\n`;\n  },\n});\n\n/** The responsive-visibility utilities as a standalone, header-wrapped stylesheet. */\nexport const responsiveUtilitiesCss: Definition[\"css\"] = responsive.css;\n"}}]},"promptRequest":{"kind":"write","toolCallId":"toolu_01KdmPT9UdhrmxqVzvJ2MtR3","intention":"Edit file","fileName":"/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/utilities/responsive/index.ts","diff":"\ndiff --git a/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/utilities/responsive/index.ts b/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/utilities/responsive/index.ts\nindex 0000000..0000000 100644\n--- a/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/utilities/responsive/index.ts\n+++ b/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/utilities/responsive/index.ts\n@@ -180,6 +180,12 @@\n  * @global\n  * @summary Viewport- or container-width show/hide classes across a themed breakpoint scale.\n  * @remarks \\`.instui-hidden-max-<bp>\\`/\\`-hidden-min-<bp>\\` hide by viewport width; \\`.instui-show-max-<bp>\\`/\\`-show-min-<bp>\\` are the inverse (hidden by default, shown only inside the range via \\`display: revert\\`); the \\`-cq-\\` variants react to a \\`.instui-container\\` ancestor's width instead, not the viewport's. Scale tiers \\`sm\\`/\\`md\\`/\\`lg\\`/\\`xl\\` mirror the IR's canonical breakpoint tokens, with a Pantoken-defined \\`xs\\` extension at \\`20em\\`; each is aliased to a long-form spelling (\\`x-small\\`\\u2013\\`x-large\\`) and a device name (\\`mobile\\`/\\`phablet\\`/\\`tablet\\`/\\`laptop\\`/\\`desktop\\`) \\u2014 both deprecated in favor of the short name \\u2014 plus the unscaled, themed \\`content\\`/\\`content-full-width\\` tiers (the main content area's max-width).\n+ * @a11y Hiding content at a breakpoint also hides it from assistive tech, so don't hide the only way to complete a task, and keep the shown and hidden versions equivalent in meaning.\n+ * @example -automatica11y\n+ * \\`\\`\\`html\n+ * <p class=\"instui-hidden-max-sm\">The full course description appears on larger screens.</p>\n+ * <p class=\"instui-show-min-sm\">The full course description appears on larger screens.</p>\n+ * \\`\\`\\`\n  * @example\n  * <div class=\"instui-hidden-max-sm\">Hidden at or below the small breakpoint.</div>\n  * <div class=\"instui-show-min-sm\">Shown only at or above the small breakpoint.</div>\n","newFileContents":"/**\n * The responsive-visibility utilities — the closest pure-CSS analogue to InstUI's `<Responsive>`:\n * viewport-width hide classes plus `-cq-` container-query variants.\n *\n * Not dual-chained onto every real component (unlike spacing/gap/layout): the alias post-processors\n * (`withSizeAliases`/`deprecatedAliasPairs` in `lib/aliases.ts`) scan this record's CSS body with\n * unanchored regexes, and this utility's selector lists (breakpoint × infix × short/long/device name)\n * are already large enough that adding ~70 more chained selectors per rule (one per real component)\n * pushes the scan into unusable-slow territory (confirmed: multi-minute hang during implementation).\n * Each rule does carry a bare `.-hidden-max-xs`-style dash modifier alongside the prefixed\n * `.instui-hidden-max-xs` class (a flat, constant-factor addition, not a per-component fan-out), so the\n * documented `@modifier` names resolve to a real selector.\n *\n * @module\n */\nimport { defineUtility, type Definition } from \"../../lib/define.ts\";\nimport { css } from \"../../lib/css.ts\";\nimport type { ComponentTheme } from \"../../lib/helpers.ts\";\nimport { breakpointEm } from \"../../lib/breakpoints.ts\";\n\n/** Short name, long-form spelling, and device name for each responsive breakpoint tier. */\nconst SCALE_TIERS: readonly [short: string, long: string, device: string][] = [\n  [\"xs\", \"x-small\", \"mobile\"],\n  [\"sm\", \"small\", \"phablet\"],\n  [\"md\", \"medium\", \"tablet\"],\n  [\"lg\", \"large\", \"laptop\"],\n  [\"xl\", \"x-large\", \"desktop\"],\n];\n\n/** Pantoken's extra-small extension, below InstUI's canonical `sm` breakpoint. */\nconst XS_BREAKPOINT_EM = \"20em\";\n\n/** `[names sharing one breakpoint value, width]` for the scale tiers — theme-invariant. */\nconst scaleBreakpoints = (): [string[], string][] =>\n  SCALE_TIERS.map(([short, long, device]) => [\n    [short, long, device],\n    short === \"xs\" ? XS_BREAKPOINT_EM : breakpointEm(`--instui-breakpoints-${short}`),\n  ]);\n\n/** The main content area's max-width, in em, per theme — hand-authored (not in the token IR). */\nconst CONTENT_BREAKPOINT_EM: Record<ComponentTheme, { content: string; contentFullWidth: string }> =\n  {\n    rebrand: { content: \"68.75em\", contentFullWidth: \"98.75em\" }, // 1100px / 1580px\n    canvas: { content: \"59.25em\", contentFullWidth: \"59.25em\" },\n    canvasHighContrast: { content: \"59.25em\", contentFullWidth: \"59.25em\" },\n  };\n\n/** The responsive-visibility utility — viewport-width hide classes plus `-cq-` container-query variants. */\nexport const responsive: Definition = defineUtility({\n  name: \"responsive\",\n  css: (p, options) => {\n    const theme = options?.theme ?? \"rebrand\";\n    const { content, contentFullWidth } = CONTENT_BREAKPOINT_EM[theme];\n    // Scale tiers get short + long-form + device-name twins; the named tiers below don't (no scale to twin against).\n    const bp: [string[], string][] = [\n      ...scaleBreakpoints(),\n      [[\"content\"], content],\n      [[\"content-full-width\"], contentFullWidth],\n    ];\n    const selectors = (prefix: string, infix: string, names: string[]): string =>\n      names.map((name) => `.${prefix}${infix}${name}, .-${infix}${name}`).join(\", \");\n    const viewport = bp\n      .map(\n        ([names, w]) =>\n          `@media (max-width: ${w}) { ${selectors(p, \"hidden-max-\", names)} { display: none !important; } }\\n` +\n          `@media (min-width: ${w}) { ${selectors(p, \"hidden-min-\", names)} { display: none !important; } }`,\n      )\n      .join(\"\\n\");\n    // Container-query variants — the true InstUI <Responsive> analogue: mark an ancestor `.<prefix>-container`\n    // and these react to ITS width, not the viewport's. Same breakpoint scale, `-cq-` infix.\n    const container = bp\n      .map(\n        ([names, w]) =>\n          `@container (max-width: ${w}) { ${selectors(p, \"cq-hidden-max-\", names)} { display: none !important; } }\\n` +\n          `@container (min-width: ${w}) { ${selectors(p, \"cq-hidden-min-\", names)} { display: none !important; } }`,\n      )\n      .join(\"\\n\");\n    // `-show-*` is the inverse of `-hidden-*`: hidden by default, `revert`ed back to its natural\n    // display only inside the matching range. `revert` (not `initial`/`unset`, which would force\n    // `inline`) restores whatever display an earlier-origin rule (UA stylesheet, or an author rule\n    // this utility doesn't override) would have set — the standard technique for a display-agnostic\n    // show utility, though it can't see a same-origin author rule's `display` if one exists.\n    const showSelector = (infix: string): string =>\n      bp.map(([names]) => selectors(p, infix, names)).join(\", \");\n    const showBase = [\"show-max-\", \"show-min-\", \"cq-show-max-\", \"cq-show-min-\"]\n      .map(showSelector)\n      .join(\", \");\n    const showViewport = bp\n      .map(\n        ([names, w]) =>\n          `@media (max-width: ${w}) { ${selectors(p, \"show-max-\", names)} { display: revert !important; } }\\n` +\n          `@media (min-width: ${w}) { ${selectors(p, \"show-min-\", names)} { display: revert !important; } }`,\n      )\n      .join(\"\\n\");\n    const showContainer = bp\n      .map(\n        ([names, w]) =>\n          `@container (max-width: ${w}) { ${selectors(p, \"cq-show-max-\", names)} { display: revert !important; } }\\n` +\n          `@container (min-width: ${w}) { ${selectors(p, \"cq-show-min-\", names)} { display: revert !important; } }`,\n      )\n      .join(\"\\n\");\n    // The @media/@container queries only define a threshold — they don't hide anything themselves\n    // (the classes below do); describe the threshold, not the visibility behavior.\n    const conditionDocs = bp\n      .map(\n        ([names, w]) =>\n          ` * @media (max-width: ${w}) — Upper bound of the \\`${names[0]}\\` breakpoint.\\n` +\n          ` * @media (min-width: ${w}) — Lower bound of the \\`${names[0]}\\` breakpoint.\\n` +\n          ` * @container (max-width: ${w}) — Upper bound of the \\`${names[0]}\\` breakpoint, evaluated against a marked container.\\n` +\n          ` * @container (min-width: ${w}) — Lower bound of the \\`${names[0]}\\` breakpoint, evaluated against a marked container.`,\n      )\n      .join(\"\\n\");\n    // Every hide class, documented; long-form/device-name twins are `@alias` aliases of the short\n    // name (cssdoc renders these the same way as the size-scale's `-size-small`/`-size-sm` aliases).\n    const modifierDocs = bp\n      .map(([names, w]) => {\n        const [short, ...aliases] = names;\n        const canonical = [\n          ` * @modifier -hidden-max-${short} — Hide when the viewport is at or below the \\`${short}\\` breakpoint (\\`${w}\\`).`,\n          ` * @modifier -hidden-min-${short} — Hide when the viewport is at or above the \\`${short}\\` breakpoint (\\`${w}\\`).`,\n          ` * @modifier -cq-hidden-max-${short} — Hide when the marked container is at or below the \\`${short}\\` breakpoint (\\`${w}\\`).`,\n          ` * @modifier -cq-hidden-min-${short} — Hide when the marked container is at or above the \\`${short}\\` breakpoint (\\`${w}\\`).`,\n        ];\n        const aliasDocs = aliases.flatMap((alias) => [\n          ` * @modifier -hidden-max-${alias} — @alias {@link -hidden-max-${short}}`,\n          ` * @modifier -hidden-min-${alias} — @alias {@link -hidden-min-${short}}`,\n          ` * @modifier -cq-hidden-max-${alias} — @alias {@link -cq-hidden-max-${short}}`,\n          ` * @modifier -cq-hidden-min-${alias} — @alias {@link -cq-hidden-min-${short}}`,\n        ]);\n        const showCanonical = [\n          ` * @modifier -show-max-${short} — Show (inverse of \\`-hidden-min-${short}\\`) when the viewport is at or below the \\`${short}\\` breakpoint (\\`${w}\\`); hidden otherwise.`,\n          ` * @modifier -show-min-${short} — Show (inverse of \\`-hidden-max-${short}\\`) when the viewport is at or above the \\`${short}\\` breakpoint (\\`${w}\\`); hidden otherwise.`,\n          ` * @modifier -cq-show-max-${short} — Show when the marked container is at or below the \\`${short}\\` breakpoint (\\`${w}\\`); hidden otherwise.`,\n          ` * @modifier -cq-show-min-${short} — Show when the marked container is at or above the \\`${short}\\` breakpoint (\\`${w}\\`); hidden otherwise.`,\n        ];\n        const showAliasDocs = aliases.flatMap((alias) => [\n          ` * @modifier -show-max-${alias} — @alias {@link -show-max-${short}}`,\n          ` * @modifier -show-min-${alias} — @alias {@link -show-min-${short}}`,\n          ` * @modifier -cq-show-max-${alias} — @alias {@link -cq-show-max-${short}}`,\n          ` * @modifier -cq-show-min-${alias} — @alias {@link -cq-show-min-${short}}`,\n        ]);\n        return [...canonical, ...aliasDocs, ...showCanonical, ...showAliasDocs].join(\"\\n\");\n      })\n      .join(\"\\n\");\n    // `@property` registers each breakpoint as an inspectable custom property (informational only —\n    // changing it does NOT move the compiled `@media`/`@container` thresholds above, since browsers\n    // can't read a custom property back into a media feature). `initial-value` must be a literal (CSS\n    // rejects `var()` there), so the scale tiers' real value is wired separately below, via `var(...)`\n    // on the same property — that's what makes `--instui-component-tray-width-*` show as consumed.\n    const properties = bp\n      .map(\n        ([names, w]) =>\n          `@property --pantoken-bp-${names[0]} { syntax: \"<length>\"; inherits: true; initial-value: ${w}; }`,\n      )\n      .join(\"\\n\");\n    const scaleSourceVars = SCALE_TIERS.map(([short]) =>\n      short === \"xs\"\n        ? `  --pantoken-bp-xs: ${XS_BREAKPOINT_EM};`\n        : `  --pantoken-bp-${short}: var(--instui-breakpoints-${short});`,\n    ).join(\"\\n\");\n    const canonicalScaleNames = new Set(SCALE_TIERS.slice(1).map(([short]) => short));\n    // Each `@property` gets real prose: scale tiers name the IR token they mirror; the two\n    // unscaled, themed tiers say so instead, since they aren't backed by a token.\n    const propertyDocs = bp\n      .map(([names, w]) => {\n        const short = names[0];\n        const source = canonicalScaleNames.has(short)\n          ? `mirrors \\`--instui-breakpoints-${short}\\``\n          : short === \"xs\"\n            ? \"hand-authored Pantoken extension (not in the token IR)\"\n            : \"hand-authored, themed (not in the token IR)\";\n        return ` * @cssproperty --pantoken-bp-${short} <length> — The \\`${short}\\` breakpoint's value (\\`${w}\\`, ${source}). Overriding it does not move the compiled \\`@media\\`/\\`@container\\` thresholds above.`;\n      })\n      .join(\"\\n\");\n    // prettier-ignore\n    return css`\n/**\n * @utility responsive\n * @selector [class*=\"-hidden-\"],[class*=\"-show-\"]\n * @global\n * @summary Viewport- or container-width show/hide classes across a themed breakpoint scale.\n * @remarks \\`.instui-hidden-max-<bp>\\`/\\`-hidden-min-<bp>\\` hide by viewport width; \\`.instui-show-max-<bp>\\`/\\`-show-min-<bp>\\` are the inverse (hidden by default, shown only inside the range via \\`display: revert\\`); the \\`-cq-\\` variants react to a \\`.instui-container\\` ancestor's width instead, not the viewport's. Scale tiers \\`sm\\`/\\`md\\`/\\`lg\\`/\\`xl\\` mirror the IR's canonical breakpoint tokens, with a Pantoken-defined \\`xs\\` extension at \\`20em\\`; each is aliased to a long-form spelling (\\`x-small\\`\\u2013\\`x-large\\`) and a device name (\\`mobile\\`/\\`phablet\\`/\\`tablet\\`/\\`laptop\\`/\\`desktop\\`) \\u2014 both deprecated in favor of the short name \\u2014 plus the unscaled, themed \\`content\\`/\\`content-full-width\\` tiers (the main content area's max-width).\n * @a11y Hiding content at a breakpoint also hides it from assistive tech, so don't hide the only way to complete a task, and keep the shown and hidden versions equivalent in meaning.\n * @example -automatica11y\n * \\`\\`\\`html\n * <p class=\"instui-hidden-max-sm\">The full course description appears on larger screens.</p>\n * <p class=\"instui-show-min-sm\">The full course description appears on larger screens.</p>\n * \\`\\`\\`\n * @example\n * <div class=\"instui-hidden-max-sm\">Hidden at or below the small breakpoint.</div>\n * <div class=\"instui-show-min-sm\">Shown only at or above the small breakpoint.</div>\n${modifierDocs}\n${conditionDocs}\n${propertyDocs}\n */\n${properties}\n:root {\n${scaleSourceVars}\n}\n${viewport}\n.${p}container { container-type: inline-size; }\n${container}\n${showBase} { display: none !important; }\n${showViewport}\n${showContainer}\n`;\n  },\n});\n\n/** The responsive-visibility utilities as a standalone, header-wrapped stylesheet. */\nexport const responsiveUtilitiesCss: Definition[\"css\"] = responsive.css;\n","canOfferSessionApproval":true,"fileEdits":[{"before":{"path":"/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/utilities/responsive/index.ts","content":"/**\n * The responsive-visibility utilities — the closest pure-CSS analogue to InstUI's `<Responsive>`:\n * viewport-width hide classes plus `-cq-` container-query variants.\n *\n * Not dual-chained onto every real component (unlike spacing/gap/layout): the alias post-processors\n * (`withSizeAliases`/`deprecatedAliasPairs` in `lib/aliases.ts`) scan this record's CSS body with\n * unanchored regexes, and this utility's selector lists (breakpoint × infix × short/long/device name)\n * are already large enough that adding ~70 more chained selectors per rule (one per real component)\n * pushes the scan into unusable-slow territory (confirmed: multi-minute hang during implementation).\n * Each rule does carry a bare `.-hidden-max-xs`-style dash modifier alongside the prefixed\n * `.instui-hidden-max-xs` class (a flat, constant-factor addition, not a per-component fan-out), so the\n * documented `@modifier` names resolve to a real selector.\n *\n * @module\n */\nimport { defineUtility, type Definition } from \"../../lib/define.ts\";\nimport { css } from \"../../lib/css.ts\";\nimport type { ComponentTheme } from \"../../lib/helpers.ts\";\nimport { breakpointEm } from \"../../lib/breakpoints.ts\";\n\n/** Short name, long-form spelling, and device name for each responsive breakpoint tier. */\nconst SCALE_TIERS: readonly [short: string, long: string, device: string][] = [\n  [\"xs\", \"x-small\", \"mobile\"],\n  [\"sm\", \"small\", \"phablet\"],\n  [\"md\", \"medium\", \"tablet\"],\n  [\"lg\", \"large\", \"laptop\"],\n  [\"xl\", \"x-large\", \"desktop\"],\n];\n\n/** Pantoken's extra-small extension, below InstUI's canonical `sm` breakpoint. */\nconst XS_BREAKPOINT_EM = \"20em\";\n\n/** `[names sharing one breakpoint value, width]` for the scale tiers — theme-invariant. */\nconst scaleBreakpoints = (): [string[], string][] =>\n  SCALE_TIERS.map(([short, long, device]) => [\n    [short, long, device],\n    short === \"xs\" ? XS_BREAKPOINT_EM : breakpointEm(`--instui-breakpoints-${short}`),\n  ]);\n\n/** The main content area's max-width, in em, per theme — hand-authored (not in the token IR). */\nconst CONTENT_BREAKPOINT_EM: Record<ComponentTheme, { content: string; contentFullWidth: string }> =\n  {\n    rebrand: { content: \"68.75em\", contentFullWidth: \"98.75em\" }, // 1100px / 1580px\n    canvas: { content: \"59.25em\", contentFullWidth: \"59.25em\" },\n    canvasHighContrast: { content: \"59.25em\", contentFullWidth: \"59.25em\" },\n  };\n\n/** The responsive-visibility utility — viewport-width hide classes plus `-cq-` container-query variants. */\nexport const responsive: Definition = defineUtility({\n  name: \"responsive\",\n  css: (p, options) => {\n    const theme = options?.theme ?? \"rebrand\";\n    const { content, contentFullWidth } = CONTENT_BREAKPOINT_EM[theme];\n    // Scale tiers get short + long-form + device-name twins; the named tiers below don't (no scale to twin against).\n    const bp: [string[], string][] = [\n      ...scaleBreakpoints(),\n      [[\"content\"], content],\n      [[\"content-full-width\"], contentFullWidth],\n    ];\n    const selectors = (prefix: string, infix: string, names: string[]): string =>\n      names.map((name) => `.${prefix}${infix}${name}, .-${infix}${name}`).join(\", \");\n    const viewport = bp\n      .map(\n        ([names, w]) =>\n          `@media (max-width: ${w}) { ${selectors(p, \"hidden-max-\", names)} { display: none !important; } }\\n` +\n          `@media (min-width: ${w}) { ${selectors(p, \"hidden-min-\", names)} { display: none !important; } }`,\n      )\n      .join(\"\\n\");\n    // Container-query variants — the true InstUI <Responsive> analogue: mark an ancestor `.<prefix>-container`\n    // and these react to ITS width, not the viewport's. Same breakpoint scale, `-cq-` infix.\n    const container = bp\n      .map(\n        ([names, w]) =>\n          `@container (max-width: ${w}) { ${selectors(p, \"cq-hidden-max-\", names)} { display: none !important; } }\\n` +\n          `@container (min-width: ${w}) { ${selectors(p, \"cq-hidden-min-\", names)} { display: none !important; } }`,\n      )\n      .join(\"\\n\");\n    // `-show-*` is the inverse of `-hidden-*`: hidden by default, `revert`ed back to its natural\n    // display only inside the matching range. `revert` (not `initial`/`unset`, which would force\n    // `inline`) restores whatever display an earlier-origin rule (UA stylesheet, or an author rule\n    // this utility doesn't override) would have set — the standard technique for a display-agnostic\n    // show utility, though it can't see a same-origin author rule's `display` if one exists.\n    const showSelector = (infix: string): string =>\n      bp.map(([names]) => selectors(p, infix, names)).join(\", \");\n    const showBase = [\"show-max-\", \"show-min-\", \"cq-show-max-\", \"cq-show-min-\"]\n      .map(showSelector)\n      .join(\", \");\n    const showViewport = bp\n      .map(\n        ([names, w]) =>\n          `@media (max-width: ${w}) { ${selectors(p, \"show-max-\", names)} { display: revert !important; } }\\n` +\n          `@media (min-width: ${w}) { ${selectors(p, \"show-min-\", names)} { display: revert !important; } }`,\n      )\n      .join(\"\\n\");\n    const showContainer = bp\n      .map(\n        ([names, w]) =>\n          `@container (max-width: ${w}) { ${selectors(p, \"cq-show-max-\", names)} { display: revert !important; } }\\n` +\n          `@container (min-width: ${w}) { ${selectors(p, \"cq-show-min-\", names)} { display: revert !important; } }`,\n      )\n      .join(\"\\n\");\n    // The @media/@container queries only define a threshold — they don't hide anything themselves\n    // (the classes below do); describe the threshold, not the visibility behavior.\n    const conditionDocs = bp\n      .map(\n        ([names, w]) =>\n          ` * @media (max-width: ${w}) — Upper bound of the \\`${names[0]}\\` breakpoint.\\n` +\n          ` * @media (min-width: ${w}) — Lower bound of the \\`${names[0]}\\` breakpoint.\\n` +\n          ` * @container (max-width: ${w}) — Upper bound of the \\`${names[0]}\\` breakpoint, evaluated against a marked container.\\n` +\n          ` * @container (min-width: ${w}) — Lower bound of the \\`${names[0]}\\` breakpoint, evaluated against a marked container.`,\n      )\n      .join(\"\\n\");\n    // Every hide class, documented; long-form/device-name twins are `@alias` aliases of the short\n    // name (cssdoc renders these the same way as the size-scale's `-size-small`/`-size-sm` aliases).\n    const modifierDocs = bp\n      .map(([names, w]) => {\n        const [short, ...aliases] = names;\n        const canonical = [\n          ` * @modifier -hidden-max-${short} — Hide when the viewport is at or below the \\`${short}\\` breakpoint (\\`${w}\\`).`,\n          ` * @modifier -hidden-min-${short} — Hide when the viewport is at or above the \\`${short}\\` breakpoint (\\`${w}\\`).`,\n          ` * @modifier -cq-hidden-max-${short} — Hide when the marked container is at or below the \\`${short}\\` breakpoint (\\`${w}\\`).`,\n          ` * @modifier -cq-hidden-min-${short} — Hide when the marked container is at or above the \\`${short}\\` breakpoint (\\`${w}\\`).`,\n        ];\n        const aliasDocs = aliases.flatMap((alias) => [\n          ` * @modifier -hidden-max-${alias} — @alias {@link -hidden-max-${short}}`,\n          ` * @modifier -hidden-min-${alias} — @alias {@link -hidden-min-${short}}`,\n          ` * @modifier -cq-hidden-max-${alias} — @alias {@link -cq-hidden-max-${short}}`,\n          ` * @modifier -cq-hidden-min-${alias} — @alias {@link -cq-hidden-min-${short}}`,\n        ]);\n        const showCanonical = [\n          ` * @modifier -show-max-${short} — Show (inverse of \\`-hidden-min-${short}\\`) when the viewport is at or below the \\`${short}\\` breakpoint (\\`${w}\\`); hidden otherwise.`,\n          ` * @modifier -show-min-${short} — Show (inverse of \\`-hidden-max-${short}\\`) when the viewport is at or above the \\`${short}\\` breakpoint (\\`${w}\\`); hidden otherwise.`,\n          ` * @modifier -cq-show-max-${short} — Show when the marked container is at or below the \\`${short}\\` breakpoint (\\`${w}\\`); hidden otherwise.`,\n          ` * @modifier -cq-show-min-${short} — Show when the marked container is at or above the \\`${short}\\` breakpoint (\\`${w}\\`); hidden otherwise.`,\n        ];\n        const showAliasDocs = aliases.flatMap((alias) => [\n          ` * @modifier -show-max-${alias} — @alias {@link -show-max-${short}}`,\n          ` * @modifier -show-min-${alias} — @alias {@link -show-min-${short}}`,\n          ` * @modifier -cq-show-max-${alias} — @alias {@link -cq-show-max-${short}}`,\n          ` * @modifier -cq-show-min-${alias} — @alias {@link -cq-show-min-${short}}`,\n        ]);\n        return [...canonical, ...aliasDocs, ...showCanonical, ...showAliasDocs].join(\"\\n\");\n      })\n      .join(\"\\n\");\n    // `@property` registers each breakpoint as an inspectable custom property (informational only —\n    // changing it does NOT move the compiled `@media`/`@container` thresholds above, since browsers\n    // can't read a custom property back into a media feature). `initial-value` must be a literal (CSS\n    // rejects `var()` there), so the scale tiers' real value is wired separately below, via `var(...)`\n    // on the same property — that's what makes `--instui-component-tray-width-*` show as consumed.\n    const properties = bp\n      .map(\n        ([names, w]) =>\n          `@property --pantoken-bp-${names[0]} { syntax: \"<length>\"; inherits: true; initial-value: ${w}; }`,\n      )\n      .join(\"\\n\");\n    const scaleSourceVars = SCALE_TIERS.map(([short]) =>\n      short === \"xs\"\n        ? `  --pantoken-bp-xs: ${XS_BREAKPOINT_EM};`\n        : `  --pantoken-bp-${short}: var(--instui-breakpoints-${short});`,\n    ).join(\"\\n\");\n    const canonicalScaleNames = new Set(SCALE_TIERS.slice(1).map(([short]) => short));\n    // Each `@property` gets real prose: scale tiers name the IR token they mirror; the two\n    // unscaled, themed tiers say so instead, since they aren't backed by a token.\n    const propertyDocs = bp\n      .map(([names, w]) => {\n        const short = names[0];\n        const source = canonicalScaleNames.has(short)\n          ? `mirrors \\`--instui-breakpoints-${short}\\``\n          : short === \"xs\"\n            ? \"hand-authored Pantoken extension (not in the token IR)\"\n            : \"hand-authored, themed (not in the token IR)\";\n        return ` * @cssproperty --pantoken-bp-${short} <length> — The \\`${short}\\` breakpoint's value (\\`${w}\\`, ${source}). Overriding it does not move the compiled \\`@media\\`/\\`@container\\` thresholds above.`;\n      })\n      .join(\"\\n\");\n    // prettier-ignore\n    return css`\n/**\n * @utility responsive\n * @selector [class*=\"-hidden-\"],[class*=\"-show-\"]\n * @global\n * @summary Viewport- or container-width show/hide classes across a themed breakpoint scale.\n * @remarks \\`.instui-hidden-max-<bp>\\`/\\`-hidden-min-<bp>\\` hide by viewport width; \\`.instui-show-max-<bp>\\`/\\`-show-min-<bp>\\` are the inverse (hidden by default, shown only inside the range via \\`display: revert\\`); the \\`-cq-\\` variants react to a \\`.instui-container\\` ancestor's width instead, not the viewport's. Scale tiers \\`sm\\`/\\`md\\`/\\`lg\\`/\\`xl\\` mirror the IR's canonical breakpoint tokens, with a Pantoken-defined \\`xs\\` extension at \\`20em\\`; each is aliased to a long-form spelling (\\`x-small\\`\\u2013\\`x-large\\`) and a device name (\\`mobile\\`/\\`phablet\\`/\\`tablet\\`/\\`laptop\\`/\\`desktop\\`) \\u2014 both deprecated in favor of the short name \\u2014 plus the unscaled, themed \\`content\\`/\\`content-full-width\\` tiers (the main content area's max-width).\n * @example\n * <div class=\"instui-hidden-max-sm\">Hidden at or below the small breakpoint.</div>\n * <div class=\"instui-show-min-sm\">Shown only at or above the small breakpoint.</div>\n${modifierDocs}\n${conditionDocs}\n${propertyDocs}\n */\n${properties}\n:root {\n${scaleSourceVars}\n}\n${viewport}\n.${p}container { container-type: inline-size; }\n${container}\n${showBase} { display: none !important; }\n${showViewport}\n${showContainer}\n`;\n  },\n});\n\n/** The responsive-visibility utilities as a standalone, header-wrapped stylesheet. */\nexport const responsiveUtilitiesCss: Definition[\"css\"] = responsive.css;\n"},"after":{"path":"/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/utilities/responsive/index.ts","content":"/**\n * The responsive-visibility utilities — the closest pure-CSS analogue to InstUI's `<Responsive>`:\n * viewport-width hide classes plus `-cq-` container-query variants.\n *\n * Not dual-chained onto every real component (unlike spacing/gap/layout): the alias post-processors\n * (`withSizeAliases`/`deprecatedAliasPairs` in `lib/aliases.ts`) scan this record's CSS body with\n * unanchored regexes, and this utility's selector lists (breakpoint × infix × short/long/device name)\n * are already large enough that adding ~70 more chained selectors per rule (one per real component)\n * pushes the scan into unusable-slow territory (confirmed: multi-minute hang during implementation).\n * Each rule does carry a bare `.-hidden-max-xs`-style dash modifier alongside the prefixed\n * `.instui-hidden-max-xs` class (a flat, constant-factor addition, not a per-component fan-out), so the\n * documented `@modifier` names resolve to a real selector.\n *\n * @module\n */\nimport { defineUtility, type Definition } from \"../../lib/define.ts\";\nimport { css } from \"../../lib/css.ts\";\nimport type { ComponentTheme } from \"../../lib/helpers.ts\";\nimport { breakpointEm } from \"../../lib/breakpoints.ts\";\n\n/** Short name, long-form spelling, and device name for each responsive breakpoint tier. */\nconst SCALE_TIERS: readonly [short: string, long: string, device: string][] = [\n  [\"xs\", \"x-small\", \"mobile\"],\n  [\"sm\", \"small\", \"phablet\"],\n  [\"md\", \"medium\", \"tablet\"],\n  [\"lg\", \"large\", \"laptop\"],\n  [\"xl\", \"x-large\", \"desktop\"],\n];\n\n/** Pantoken's extra-small extension, below InstUI's canonical `sm` breakpoint. */\nconst XS_BREAKPOINT_EM = \"20em\";\n\n/** `[names sharing one breakpoint value, width]` for the scale tiers — theme-invariant. */\nconst scaleBreakpoints = (): [string[], string][] =>\n  SCALE_TIERS.map(([short, long, device]) => [\n    [short, long, device],\n    short === \"xs\" ? XS_BREAKPOINT_EM : breakpointEm(`--instui-breakpoints-${short}`),\n  ]);\n\n/** The main content area's max-width, in em, per theme — hand-authored (not in the token IR). */\nconst CONTENT_BREAKPOINT_EM: Record<ComponentTheme, { content: string; contentFullWidth: string }> =\n  {\n    rebrand: { content: \"68.75em\", contentFullWidth: \"98.75em\" }, // 1100px / 1580px\n    canvas: { content: \"59.25em\", contentFullWidth: \"59.25em\" },\n    canvasHighContrast: { content: \"59.25em\", contentFullWidth: \"59.25em\" },\n  };\n\n/** The responsive-visibility utility — viewport-width hide classes plus `-cq-` container-query variants. */\nexport const responsive: Definition = defineUtility({\n  name: \"responsive\",\n  css: (p, options) => {\n    const theme = options?.theme ?? \"rebrand\";\n    const { content, contentFullWidth } = CONTENT_BREAKPOINT_EM[theme];\n    // Scale tiers get short + long-form + device-name twins; the named tiers below don't (no scale to twin against).\n    const bp: [string[], string][] = [\n      ...scaleBreakpoints(),\n      [[\"content\"], content],\n      [[\"content-full-width\"], contentFullWidth],\n    ];\n    const selectors = (prefix: string, infix: string, names: string[]): string =>\n      names.map((name) => `.${prefix}${infix}${name}, .-${infix}${name}`).join(\", \");\n    const viewport = bp\n      .map(\n        ([names, w]) =>\n          `@media (max-width: ${w}) { ${selectors(p, \"hidden-max-\", names)} { display: none !important; } }\\n` +\n          `@media (min-width: ${w}) { ${selectors(p, \"hidden-min-\", names)} { display: none !important; } }`,\n      )\n      .join(\"\\n\");\n    // Container-query variants — the true InstUI <Responsive> analogue: mark an ancestor `.<prefix>-container`\n    // and these react to ITS width, not the viewport's. Same breakpoint scale, `-cq-` infix.\n    const container = bp\n      .map(\n        ([names, w]) =>\n          `@container (max-width: ${w}) { ${selectors(p, \"cq-hidden-max-\", names)} { display: none !important; } }\\n` +\n          `@container (min-width: ${w}) { ${selectors(p, \"cq-hidden-min-\", names)} { display: none !important; } }`,\n      )\n      .join(\"\\n\");\n    // `-show-*` is the inverse of `-hidden-*`: hidden by default, `revert`ed back to its natural\n    // display only inside the matching range. `revert` (not `initial`/`unset`, which would force\n    // `inline`) restores whatever display an earlier-origin rule (UA stylesheet, or an author rule\n    // this utility doesn't override) would have set — the standard technique for a display-agnostic\n    // show utility, though it can't see a same-origin author rule's `display` if one exists.\n    const showSelector = (infix: string): string =>\n      bp.map(([names]) => selectors(p, infix, names)).join(\", \");\n    const showBase = [\"show-max-\", \"show-min-\", \"cq-show-max-\", \"cq-show-min-\"]\n      .map(showSelector)\n      .join(\", \");\n    const showViewport = bp\n      .map(\n        ([names, w]) =>\n          `@media (max-width: ${w}) { ${selectors(p, \"show-max-\", names)} { display: revert !important; } }\\n` +\n          `@media (min-width: ${w}) { ${selectors(p, \"show-min-\", names)} { display: revert !important; } }`,\n      )\n      .join(\"\\n\");\n    const showContainer = bp\n      .map(\n        ([names, w]) =>\n          `@container (max-width: ${w}) { ${selectors(p, \"cq-show-max-\", names)} { display: revert !important; } }\\n` +\n          `@container (min-width: ${w}) { ${selectors(p, \"cq-show-min-\", names)} { display: revert !important; } }`,\n      )\n      .join(\"\\n\");\n    // The @media/@container queries only define a threshold — they don't hide anything themselves\n    // (the classes below do); describe the threshold, not the visibility behavior.\n    const conditionDocs = bp\n      .map(\n        ([names, w]) =>\n          ` * @media (max-width: ${w}) — Upper bound of the \\`${names[0]}\\` breakpoint.\\n` +\n          ` * @media (min-width: ${w}) — Lower bound of the \\`${names[0]}\\` breakpoint.\\n` +\n          ` * @container (max-width: ${w}) — Upper bound of the \\`${names[0]}\\` breakpoint, evaluated against a marked container.\\n` +\n          ` * @container (min-width: ${w}) — Lower bound of the \\`${names[0]}\\` breakpoint, evaluated against a marked container.`,\n      )\n      .join(\"\\n\");\n    // Every hide class, documented; long-form/device-name twins are `@alias` aliases of the short\n    // name (cssdoc renders these the same way as the size-scale's `-size-small`/`-size-sm` aliases).\n    const modifierDocs = bp\n      .map(([names, w]) => {\n        const [short, ...aliases] = names;\n        const canonical = [\n          ` * @modifier -hidden-max-${short} — Hide when the viewport is at or below the \\`${short}\\` breakpoint (\\`${w}\\`).`,\n          ` * @modifier -hidden-min-${short} — Hide when the viewport is at or above the \\`${short}\\` breakpoint (\\`${w}\\`).`,\n          ` * @modifier -cq-hidden-max-${short} — Hide when the marked container is at or below the \\`${short}\\` breakpoint (\\`${w}\\`).`,\n          ` * @modifier -cq-hidden-min-${short} — Hide when the marked container is at or above the \\`${short}\\` breakpoint (\\`${w}\\`).`,\n        ];\n        const aliasDocs = aliases.flatMap((alias) => [\n          ` * @modifier -hidden-max-${alias} — @alias {@link -hidden-max-${short}}`,\n          ` * @modifier -hidden-min-${alias} — @alias {@link -hidden-min-${short}}`,\n          ` * @modifier -cq-hidden-max-${alias} — @alias {@link -cq-hidden-max-${short}}`,\n          ` * @modifier -cq-hidden-min-${alias} — @alias {@link -cq-hidden-min-${short}}`,\n        ]);\n        const showCanonical = [\n          ` * @modifier -show-max-${short} — Show (inverse of \\`-hidden-min-${short}\\`) when the viewport is at or below the \\`${short}\\` breakpoint (\\`${w}\\`); hidden otherwise.`,\n          ` * @modifier -show-min-${short} — Show (inverse of \\`-hidden-max-${short}\\`) when the viewport is at or above the \\`${short}\\` breakpoint (\\`${w}\\`); hidden otherwise.`,\n          ` * @modifier -cq-show-max-${short} — Show when the marked container is at or below the \\`${short}\\` breakpoint (\\`${w}\\`); hidden otherwise.`,\n          ` * @modifier -cq-show-min-${short} — Show when the marked container is at or above the \\`${short}\\` breakpoint (\\`${w}\\`); hidden otherwise.`,\n        ];\n        const showAliasDocs = aliases.flatMap((alias) => [\n          ` * @modifier -show-max-${alias} — @alias {@link -show-max-${short}}`,\n          ` * @modifier -show-min-${alias} — @alias {@link -show-min-${short}}`,\n          ` * @modifier -cq-show-max-${alias} — @alias {@link -cq-show-max-${short}}`,\n          ` * @modifier -cq-show-min-${alias} — @alias {@link -cq-show-min-${short}}`,\n        ]);\n        return [...canonical, ...aliasDocs, ...showCanonical, ...showAliasDocs].join(\"\\n\");\n      })\n      .join(\"\\n\");\n    // `@property` registers each breakpoint as an inspectable custom property (informational only —\n    // changing it does NOT move the compiled `@media`/`@container` thresholds above, since browsers\n    // can't read a custom property back into a media feature). `initial-value` must be a literal (CSS\n    // rejects `var()` there), so the scale tiers' real value is wired separately below, via `var(...)`\n    // on the same property — that's what makes `--instui-component-tray-width-*` show as consumed.\n    const properties = bp\n      .map(\n        ([names, w]) =>\n          `@property --pantoken-bp-${names[0]} { syntax: \"<length>\"; inherits: true; initial-value: ${w}; }`,\n      )\n      .join(\"\\n\");\n    const scaleSourceVars = SCALE_TIERS.map(([short]) =>\n      short === \"xs\"\n        ? `  --pantoken-bp-xs: ${XS_BREAKPOINT_EM};`\n        : `  --pantoken-bp-${short}: var(--instui-breakpoints-${short});`,\n    ).join(\"\\n\");\n    const canonicalScaleNames = new Set(SCALE_TIERS.slice(1).map(([short]) => short));\n    // Each `@property` gets real prose: scale tiers name the IR token they mirror; the two\n    // unscaled, themed tiers say so instead, since they aren't backed by a token.\n    const propertyDocs = bp\n      .map(([names, w]) => {\n        const short = names[0];\n        const source = canonicalScaleNames.has(short)\n          ? `mirrors \\`--instui-breakpoints-${short}\\``\n          : short === \"xs\"\n            ? \"hand-authored Pantoken extension (not in the token IR)\"\n            : \"hand-authored, themed (not in the token IR)\";\n        return ` * @cssproperty --pantoken-bp-${short} <length> — The \\`${short}\\` breakpoint's value (\\`${w}\\`, ${source}). Overriding it does not move the compiled \\`@media\\`/\\`@container\\` thresholds above.`;\n      })\n      .join(\"\\n\");\n    // prettier-ignore\n    return css`\n/**\n * @utility responsive\n * @selector [class*=\"-hidden-\"],[class*=\"-show-\"]\n * @global\n * @summary Viewport- or container-width show/hide classes across a themed breakpoint scale.\n * @remarks \\`.instui-hidden-max-<bp>\\`/\\`-hidden-min-<bp>\\` hide by viewport width; \\`.instui-show-max-<bp>\\`/\\`-show-min-<bp>\\` are the inverse (hidden by default, shown only inside the range via \\`display: revert\\`); the \\`-cq-\\` variants react to a \\`.instui-container\\` ancestor's width instead, not the viewport's. Scale tiers \\`sm\\`/\\`md\\`/\\`lg\\`/\\`xl\\` mirror the IR's canonical breakpoint tokens, with a Pantoken-defined \\`xs\\` extension at \\`20em\\`; each is aliased to a long-form spelling (\\`x-small\\`\\u2013\\`x-large\\`) and a device name (\\`mobile\\`/\\`phablet\\`/\\`tablet\\`/\\`laptop\\`/\\`desktop\\`) \\u2014 both deprecated in favor of the short name \\u2014 plus the unscaled, themed \\`content\\`/\\`content-full-width\\` tiers (the main content area's max-width).\n * @a11y Hiding content at a breakpoint also hides it from assistive tech, so don't hide the only way to complete a task, and keep the shown and hidden versions equivalent in meaning.\n * @example -automatica11y\n * \\`\\`\\`html\n * <p class=\"instui-hidden-max-sm\">The full course description appears on larger screens.</p>\n * <p class=\"instui-show-min-sm\">The full course description appears on larger screens.</p>\n * \\`\\`\\`\n * @example\n * <div class=\"instui-hidden-max-sm\">Hidden at or below the small breakpoint.</div>\n * <div class=\"instui-show-min-sm\">Shown only at or above the small breakpoint.</div>\n${modifierDocs}\n${conditionDocs}\n${propertyDocs}\n */\n${properties}\n:root {\n${scaleSourceVars}\n}\n${viewport}\n.${p}container { container-type: inline-size; }\n${container}\n${showBase} { display: none !important; }\n${showViewport}\n${showContainer}\n`;\n  },\n});\n\n/** The responsive-visibility utilities as a standalone, header-wrapped stylesheet. */\nexport const responsiveUtilitiesCss: Definition[\"css\"] = responsive.css;\n"}}],"_permissionRequestSessionId":"cf8db52f-0f27-4d51-8f45-3f9af32eb056","assistedApproval":{"recommendation":"approve","reason":"Adds accessibility guidance and an audit example to an in-scope utility source file.","model":"gpt-6-luna","evaluation":{"reasonCode":"judge-verdict","judgeStatus":"completed","evaluationStage":"judge","judgeAttempted":true}}},"agentMode":"interactive","permissionMode":"assisted","ownerSessionId":"cf8db52f-0f27-4d51-8f4