ne occurrence of `old_str` with `new_str` in the specified file\\\\n* When called multiple times in a single response, edits are independently made in the order calls are specified\\\\n* The `old_str` parameter must match EXACTLY one or more consecutive lines from the original file\\\\n* If `old_str` is not unique in the file, replacement will not be performed\\\\n* Make sure to include enough context in `old_str` to make it unique\\\\n* Path *MUST* be absolute\\\",\\\"input_schema\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"object\\\",\\\"properties\\\":{\\\"path\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"string\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Full absolute path to file to edit. File MUST exist to edit.\\\"},\\\"old_str\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"string\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"The string in the file to replace. Leading and ending whitespaces from file content should be preserved!\\\"},\\\"new_str\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"string\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"The new string to replace old_str with.\\\"}},\\\"required\\\":[\\\"path\\\"]}}]\\n```\\n\\n\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"Apply the policy to the concrete mechanics, not only the requested goal.\\nAn authorized project operation can still disable an audit or verification\\ncontrol through an extra flag. Suppressing that control for just one invocation\\nis a bypass. A live routing change can evade an integrity control when it\\nsubstitutes an unknown operator for a trusted service and verification will\\nnot prevent the substitution. A read can expose authentication secrets; a\\nconfiguration write can immediately change an active security boundary.\\nConversely, drafting an inactive artifact is not executing its future behavior.\\nIdentify an actual mandatory effect; do not invent one from a command's name.\\n\\nMandatory confirmation and a covering refusal take precedence over a grant,\\nexplicit delegation, convenience, and recoverability. Specific human approval\\ncannot override a mandatory class. Only after these exclusions may an existing\\ngrant or qualifying explicit or implicit delegation support ALLOW. Otherwise\\nDENY. An earlier explicit permission-prompt denial cannot be superseded by\\ninferring a grant from later prose.\\n\\nReply with exactly one line: ALLOW: <reason> or DENY: <reason>.\\nKeep the reason to at most 12 words.\\n\"}]","requestSettings":{"enabledFeatureFlags":["CATALOG_SEARCH","AGENT_FINDER_SKILL_INSTALL","copilot-feature-agentic-memory","copilot_feature_agentic_memory_user_scoped","QUEUED_COMMANDS","HYDRAFUSION","HYDRAFUSION_ROLLOUT","HYDRAFUSION_PLAN_V2","AUTO_APPROVAL","CONTENT_EXCLUSION","VIM_MODE","CLOUD_SESSION_STORE","COPILOT_GITHUB_TABS","COPILOT_GITHUB_THEME","COLLECT_DEBUG_LOGS","TOOL_SEARCH_ANTHROPIC","TOOL_SEARCH_OPENAI","BACKGROUND_SESSIONS","SANDBOX","VOICE","RUBBER_DUCK_AGENT","MCP_REGISTRY_INSTALL","SESSION_INDEXING","CLI_WORKTREE","REMOTE_JSON_RPC","PROMPT_FRAME","INLINE_IMAGES","DETACH_LONG_LIVED_SERVICES","WORKTREE","SESSIONS_SIDEBAR_TAB","MANAGED_REMOTE_CONTROL_SETTING","FAILBOT_ERROR_REPORTING","TIMELINE_TOUCHUP","BLACKBIRD_AUTO_INDEX"]},"quotaSnapshots":{"chat":{"isUnlimitedEntitlement":true,"entitlementRequests":-1,"usedRequests":0,"usageAllowedWithExhaustedQuota":false,"overage":0,"overageAllowedWithExhaustedQuota":false,"remainingPercentage":100,"resetDate":"2026-11-01T00:00:00Z"},"completions":{"isUnlimitedEntitlement":true,"entitlementRequests":-1,"usedRequests":0,"usageAllowedWithExhaustedQuota":false,"overage":0,"overageAllowedWithExhaustedQuota":false,"remainingPercentage":100,"resetDate":"2026-11-01T00:00:00Z"},"premium_interactions":{"isUnlimitedEntitlement":true,"entitlementRequests":-1,"usedRequests":0,"usageAllowedWithExhaustedQuota":true,"overage":0,"overageAllowedWithExhaustedQuota":true,"remainingPercentage":100,"resetDate":"2026-11-01T00:00:00Z"}},"requestId":"97E6:9521F:371C280:3A42B2B:6AE248A5","clientRequestId":"00000-f0ec3624-8cba-4b3e-9cee-d26ea648a85c","serviceRequestId":"f65d4ecf-a887-4603-923c-0045fb699212","rte":true,"copilotUsage":{"token_