 @example -automatica11y\\\\n * \\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`html\\\\n * <p class=\\\\\\\"--truncate --max-lines-2\\\\\\\" style=\\\\\\\"inline-size: 16rem\\\\\\\">Quarterly planning notes for the curriculum review committee, including agenda items and follow-up actions.</p>\\\\n * \\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`\\\\n * @related text — Body typography that this truncates.\\\"}\\n[tool bash -> success] args={\\\"command\\\":\\\"cd /Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/utilities && for u in overflow spacing gap layout position stacking cursor mask; do echo \\\\\\\"=== $u\\\\\\\"; grep -n \\\\\\\"@example\\\\\\\" -B3 -A4 $u/index.ts | head -14; done; grep -n \\\\\\\"@modifier\\\\\\\" overflow/index.ts position/index.ts cursor/index.ts spacing/index.ts gap/index.ts | cut -c1-150 | head -30\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"View anchors for edits\\\"}\\n[tool edit -> success] args={\\\"new_str\\\":\\\" * @a11y A scrollable region must work from the keyboard: give it \\\\\\\\`tabindex=\\\\\\\"0\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\`, a role, and an accessible name (or make sure it contains a focusable control). Don't use \\\\\\\\`hidden\\\\\\\\` or \\\\\\\\`clip\\\\\\\\` to cut off content people need to read.\\\\n * @example -automatica11y\\\\n * \\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`html\\\\n * <div class=\\\\\\\"--overflow-y-auto\\\\\\\" tabindex=\\\\\\\"0\\\\\\\" role=\\\\\\\"region\\\\\\\" aria-label=\\\\\\\"Release notes\\\\\\\" style=\\\\\\\"block-size: 5rem\\\\\\\">\\\\n * <p>Version 2.4 adds keyboard shortcuts for the gradebook.</p>\\\\n * <p>Version 2.3 fixes focus order in the course menu.</p>\\\\n * <p>Version 2.2 improves contrast in dark mode.</p>\\\\n * <p>Version 2.1 updates the file upload messages.</p>\\\\n * </div>\\\\n * \\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`\\\\n * @example\\\\n * <div class=\\\\\\\"--overflow-y-auto\\\\\\\">…</div>\\\",\\\"old_str\\\":\\\" * @example\\\\n * <div class=\\\\\\\"--overflow-y-auto\\\\\\\">…</div>\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/utilities/overflow/index.ts\\\"}\\n[tool edit -> success] args={\\\"new_str\\\":\\\" * @a11y Spacing is visual only: use it to keep text and controls from crowding, not to convey structure — use headings, lists, and landmarks for that. Leave enough space around interactive targets for WCAG 2.5.8, and don't rely on fixed spacing that breaks when users increase text spacing.\\\\n * @example -automatica11y\\\\n * \\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`html\\\\n * <div class=\\\\\\\"--p-md --mt-lg\\\\\\\">\\\\n * <h2>Office hours</h2>\\\\n * <p>Mondays and Wednesdays, 2–4 pm.</p>\\\\n * </div>\\\\n * \\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`\\\\n * @example\\\\n * <div class=\\\\\\\"--p-md --mt-lg\\\\\\\">Padded box with a large top margin.</div>\\\",\\\"old_str\\\":\\\" * @example\\\\n * <div class=\\\\\\\"--p-md --mt-lg\\\\\\\">Padded box with a large top margin.</div>\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/utilities/spacing/index.ts\\\"}\\n[tool edit -> success] args={\\\"new_str\\\":\\\" * @a11y A gap changes spacing only; reading and focus order still follow the DOM. Keep gaps between interactive controls large enough to meet WCAG 2.5.8 target spacing.\\\\n * @example -automatica11y\\\\n * \\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`html\\\\n * <div class=\\\\\\\"--display-flex --gap-sm\\\\\\\">\\\\n * <button class=\\\\\\\"instui-button\\\\\\\">Save</button>\\\\n * <button class=\\\\\\\"instui-button\\\\\\\">Cancel</button>\\\\n * </div>\\\\n * \\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`\\\\n * @example\\\\n * <div class=\\\\\\\"--display-flex --gap-sm\\\\\\\">\\\",\\\"old_str\\\":\\\" * @example\\\\n * <div class=\\\\\\\"--display-flex --gap-sm\\\\\\\">\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/utilities/gap/index.ts\\\"}\\n[tool edit -> success] args={\\\"new_str\\\":\\\" * @a11y \\\\\\\\`--display-none\\\\\\\\` removes an element from the accessibility tree as well as the screen, so use it only for content nobody needs. Flex and grid layout can't reorder content for assistive tech; keep the DOM order meaningful, and don't center or justify long passages of text.\\\\n * @example -automatica11y\\\\n * \\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`html\\\\n * <div class=\\\\\\\"--display-flex --text-align-center\\\\\\\">\\\\n * <span>Course</span>\\\\n * <span>Grades</span>\\\\n * </div>\\\\n * \\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`\\\\n * @example\\\\n * <div class=\\\\\\\"--display-flex --text-align-center\\\\\\\">\\\",\\\"old_str\\\":\\\" * @example\\\\n * <div class=\\\\\\\"--display-flex --text-align-center\\\\\\\">\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/utilities/layout/index.ts\\\"}\\n[tool edit -> success] args={\\\"new_str\\\":\\\" * @a11y Positioning changes where content appears, not where it sits in the DOM: keep the visual order matching the reading and focus order, and don't let positioned content cover a focused control.\\\\n * @example -automatica11y\\\\n * \\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`html\\\\n * <div class=\\\\\\\"--position-relative\\\\\\\">\\\\n * <p>Positioned content stays in reading order.</p>\\\\n * </div>\\\\n * \\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`\\\\n * @example\\\\n * <div class=\\\\\\\"--position-relative\\\\\\\">…</div>\\\",\\\"old_str\\\":\\\" * @example\\\\n * <div class=\\\\\\\"--position-relative\\\\\\\">…</div>\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/utilities/position/index.ts\\\"}\\n[tool edit -> success] args={\\\"new_str\\\":\\\" * @a11y Stacking order is visual only: a layered surface that covers focusable content hides the focus indicator. Overlays that take over the page also need focus management and an accessible name.\\\\n * @example -automatica11y\\\\n * \\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`html\\\\n * <div class=\\\\\\\"--stack-above\\\\\\\">\\\\n * <p>Content raised above the default flow.</p>\\\\n * </div>\\\\n * \\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`\\\\n * @example\\\\n * <div class=\\\\\\\"--stack-topmost\\\\\\\">Always on top.</div>\\\",\\\"old_str\\\":\\\" * @example\\\\n * <div class=\\\\\\\"--stack-topmost\\\\\\\">Always on top.</div>\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/utilities/stacking/index.ts\\\"}\\n[tool edit -> success] args={\\\"new_str\\\":\\\" * @a11y The cursor only affects pointer users; a pointer cursor doesn't make an element operable. Put it on native controls (\\\\\\\\`button\\\\\\\\`, \\\\\\\\`a\\\\\\\\`), and never use \\\\\\\\`--cursor-not-allowed\\\\\\\\` or \\\\\\\\`--cursor-wait\\\\\\\\` as the only sign that something is disabled or busy.\\\\n * @example -automatica11y\\\\n * \\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`html\\\\n * <button class=\\\\\\\"instui-button --cursor-pointer\\\\\\\">Open details</button>\\\\n * \\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`\\\\n * @example\\\\n * <div class=\\\\\\\"--cursor-pointer\\\\\\\">…</div>\\\",\\\"old_str\\\":\\\" * @example\\\\n * <div class=\\\\\\\"--cursor-pointer\\\\\\\">…</div>\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/utilities/cursor/index.ts\\\"}\\n[tool edit -> success] args={\\\"new_str\\\":\\\" * @a11y A mask covers content visually but doesn't block assistive tech or the keyboard: make the covered region \\\\\\\\`inert\\\\\\\\` (or mark it \\\\\\\\`aria-busy\\\\\\\\`), keep the mask's own message as real text, and don't hide the focus indicator behind it.\\\\n * @example -automatica11y\\\\n * \\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`html\\\\n * <div class=\\\\\\\"--position-relative\\\\\\\" style=\\\\\\\"min-block-size: 4rem\\\\\\\">\\\\n * <p>Gradebook</p>\\\\n * <div class=\\\\\\\"--mask-overlay\\\\\\\" role=\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\">Loading grades…</div>\\\\n * </div>\\\\n * \\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`\\\\n * @example\\\\n * <button class=\\\\\\\"instui-button --mask-overlay\\\\\\\">…</button>\\\",\\\"old_str\\\":\\\" * @example\\\\n * <button class=\\\\\\\"instui-button --mask-overlay\\\\\\\">…</button>\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/utilities/mask/index.ts\\\"}\\n[tool edit -> success] args={\\\"new_str\\\":\\\" * @a11y Hiding content at a breakpoint also hides it from assistive tech, so don't hide the only way to complete a task, and keep the shown and hidden versions equivalent in meaning.\\\\n * @example -automatica11y\\\\n * \\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`html\\\\n * <p class=\\\\\\\"instui-hidden-max-sm\\\\\\\">The full course description appears on larger screens.</p>\\\\n * <p class=\\\\\\\"instui-show-min-sm\\\\\\\">The full course description appears on larger screens.</p>\\\\n * \\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`\\\\n * @example\\\\n * <div class=\\\\\\\"instui-hidden-max-sm\\\\\\\">Hidden at or below the small breakpoint.</div>\\\",\\\"old_str\\\":\\\" * @example\\\\n * <div class=\\\\\\\"instui-hidden-max-sm\\\\\\\">Hidden at or below the small breakpoint.</div>\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/utilities/responsive/index.ts\\\"}\\n[tool edit -> success] args={\\\"new_str\\\":\\\" * @example -automatica11y\\\\n * ```html\\\\n * <div class=\\\\\\\"instui-transition -transition-fade-entered\\\\\\\">Animated content</div>\\\\n * ```\\\\n * @example\\\\n * <div class=\\\\\\\"instui-transition -transition-fade-entering\\\\\\\">Animated content</div>\\\",\\\"old_str\\\":\\\" * @example\\\\n * <div class=\\\\\\\"instui-transition -transition-fade-entering\\\\\\\">Animated content</div>\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/utilities/transition/transition.css\\\"}\\n[tool edit -> success] args={\\\"new_str\\\":\\\" * @example -automatica11y\\\\n * ```html\\\\n * <div class=\\\\\\\"instui-view -with-visual-debug\\\\\\\">\\\\n * <span>Outlined child.</span>\\\\n * </div>\\\\n * ```\\\\n * @example\\\\n * <div class=\\\\\\\"instui-view -with-visual-debug\\\\\\\">\\\",\\\"old_str\\\":\\\" * @example\\\\n * <div class=\\\\\\\"instui-view -with-visual-debug\\\\\\\">\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/utilities/visual-deb