ew_str\\\":\\\" expect(snapshot.records[\\\\\\\"agent-shell\\\\\\\"]).toHaveLength(4);\\\\n expect(snapshot.records[\\\\\\\"ai-gradient\\\\\\\"]).toBeUndefined();\\\",\\\"old_str\\\":\\\" expect(snapshot.records[\\\\\\\"agent-shell\\\\\\\"]).toBeUndefined();\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/docs/scripts/accessibility-evidence.test.ts\\\"}\\n[tool bash -> success] args={\\\"command\\\":\\\"cd /Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken && vp test run docs/scripts/accessibility-evidence.test.ts 2>&1 | grep -E \\\\\\\"Tests |FAIL|Assertion\\\\\\\"; git add -- docs/scripts/accessibility-evidence.test.ts && git commit -q -m \\\\\\\"test(docs): expect the custom components in the snapshot\\\\\\\" -m \\\\\\\"Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\\\\\\\" 2>&1 | tail -1; git log --oneline -1\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Fix and commit test\\\",\\\"initial_wait\\\":120}\\n[assistant] `agent-shell` and five other custom-components records are now audited, and their API pages show real audit tables instead of \\\"Not audited\\\". I did not look at the pages in a browser. The full audit and the importer tests pass. - **What was wrong:** the audit only covered the core records, so none of the plugin components were ever included. - **What's now covered:** `agent-shell`, `banner`, `button-set`, `logo`, `segmented-control` and `skeleton-loader`. The pages load the plugin's stylesheet, and the list lives in `formats/components/scripts/audit-plugin-components.ts`. - **agent-shell:** it was the only one of the six missing guidance, so I added an `@a11y` block and an `-automatica11y` example (a labelled `<section>`). The other five already had both. - **Guard test:** a new test requires every plugin record to have `@a11y` text and an audit example. - **Snapshot:** I re-ran the whole audit and re-imported it. The snapshot went from 76 to 82 records. A few things you might trip over: - **Left out:** the plugin's `ai-gradient` is still unaudited. It's a utility, not a component, and it has no `@a11y` text or examples. It also has the same name as a core record. Say if you want it included. `card` was already covered through core, and `segmented-control.segment` has no page of its own. - **Not covered:** the layouts plugin pages (callout, hero and similar) are still \\\"Not audited\\\", per your choice of custom-components only. - **Changeset:** I added one for `@pantoken/plugin-custom-components`. It covers the `agent-shell` guidance. - **Snapshot diff:** the snapshot file shows a large diff because the full run replaced all of its contents. - **CI:** I haven't re-run it on any of these changes.\\n[human #20] layout plugin doesn't need to be covered. for both components and custom-components go through the utilities, declarations, etc. and add those audits where applicable.\\n[context] <current_datetime>2026-10-28T13:08:05.474-06:00</current_datetime> layout plugin doesn't need to be covered. for both components and custom-components go through the utilities, declarations, etc. and add those audits where applicable.\\n[tool bash -> success] args={\\\"command\\\":\\\"cd /Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken && grep -L \\\\\\\"pantoken-a11y-table\\\\\\\" docs/api/css/*.md | xargs -n1 basename; sed -n 1,60p formats/components/src/components/index.ts | head -60; cat formats/components/src/utilities/index.ts | head -40; ls formats/components/src/declarations plugins/pantoken/custom-components/src/declarations\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"List unaudited pages and source buckets\\\"}\\n[tool bash -> success] args={\\\"command\\\":\\\"cd /Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken && head -5 docs/api/css/color.md docs/api/css/primitives.md docs/api/css/base.md docs/api/css/breakpoints.md docs/api/css/maskglobal.md | cut -c1-200; cat formats/components/src/rules/index.ts | grep -v \\\\\\\"^ \\\\\\\\*\\\\\\\\|^/\\\\\\\\*\\\\\\\" ; cat formats/components/src/declarations/index.ts | grep -v \\\\\\\"^ \\\\\\\\*\\\\\\\\|^/\\\\\\\\*\\\\\\\"; cd formats/