ssibility-evidence.test.ts\\\"}\\n[tool edit -> success] args={\\\"new_str\\\":\\\" expect(snapshot.records[\\\\\\\"agent-shell\\\\\\\"]).toHaveLength(4);\\\\n expect(snapshot.records[\\\\\\\"ai-gradient\\\\\\\"]).toBeUndefined();\\\",\\\"old_str\\\":\\\" expect(snapshot.records[\\\\\\\"agent-shell\\\\\\\"]).toBeUndefined();\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/docs/scripts/accessibility-evidence.test.ts\\\"}\\n[tool bash -> success] args={\\\"command\\\":\\\"cd /Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken && vp test run docs/scripts/accessibility-evidence.test.ts 2>&1 | grep -E \\\\\\\"Tests |FAIL|Assertion\\\\\\\"; git add -- docs/scripts/accessibility-evidence.test.ts && git commit -q -m \\\\\\\"test(docs): expect the custom components in the snapshot\\\\\\\" -m \\\\\\\"Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\\\\\\\" 2>&1 | tail -1; git log --oneline -1\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Fix and commit test\\\",\\\"initial_wait\\\":120}\\n[assistant] `agent-shell` and five other custom-components records are now audited, and their API pages show real audit tables instead of \\\"Not audited\\\". I did not look at the pages in a browser. The full audit and the importer tests pass. - **What was wrong:** the audit only covered the core records, so none of the plugin components were ever included. - **What's now covered:** `agent-shell`, `banner`, `button-set`, `logo`, `segmented-control` and `skeleton-loader`. The pages load the plugin's stylesheet, and the list lives in `formats/components/scripts/audit-plugin-components.ts`. - **agent-shell:** it was the only one of the six missing guidance, so I added an `@a11y` block and an `-automatica11y` example (a labelled `<section>`). The other five already had both. - **Guard test:** a new test requires every plugin record to have `@a11y` text and an audit example. - **Snapshot:** I re-ran the whole audit and re-imported it. The snapshot went from 76 to 82 records. A few things you might trip over: - **Left out:** the plugin's `ai-gradient` is still unaudited. It's a utility, not a component, and it has no `@a11y` text or examples. It also has the same name as a core record. Say if you want it included. `card` was already covered through core, and `segmented-control.segment` has no page of its own. - **Not covered:** the layouts plugin pages (callout, hero and similar) are still \\\"Not audited\\\", per your choice of custom-components only. - **Changeset:** I added one for `@pantoken/plugin-custom-components`. It covers the `agent-shell` guidance. - **Snapshot diff:** the snapshot file shows a large diff because the full run replaced all of its contents. - **CI:** I haven't re-run it on any of these changes.\\n[human #20] layout plugin doesn't need to be covered. for both components and custom-components go through the utilities, declarations, etc. and add those audits where applicable.\\n[context] <current_datetime>2026-10-28T13:08:05.474-06:00</current_datetime> layout plugin doesn't need to be covered. for both components and custom-components go through the utilities, declarations, etc. and add those audits where applicable.\\n[tool bash -> success] args={\\\"command\\\":\\\"cd /Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken && grep -L \\\\\\\"pantoken-a11y-table\\\\\\\" docs/api/css/*.md | xargs -n1 basename; sed -n 1,60p formats/components/src/components/index.ts | head -60; cat formats/components/src/utilities/index.ts | head -40; ls formats/components/src/declarations plugins/pantoken/custom-components/src/declarations\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"List unaudited pages and source buckets\\\"}\\n[tool bash -> success] args={\\\"command\\\":\\\"cd /Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken && head -5 docs/api/css/color.md docs/api/css/primitives.md docs/api/css/base.md docs/api/css/breakpoints.md docs/api/css/maskglobal.md | cut -c1-200; cat formats/components/src/rules/index.ts | grep -v \\\\\\\"^ \\\\\\\\*\\\\\\\\|^/\\\\\\\\*\\\\\\\" ; cat formats/components/src/declarations/index.ts | grep -v \\\\\\\"^ \\\\\\\\*\\\\\\\\|^/\\\\\\\\*\\\\\\\"; cd formats/components/src; for f in utilities/*/*.css rules/*/*.css declarations/*/*.css; do echo \\\\\\\"$f a11y=$(grep -c '@a11y\\\\\\\\|@accessibility' $f) ex=$(grep -c '@example' $f) auto=$(grep -c automatica11y $f)\\\\\\\"; done\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Survey records for a11y and examples\\\"}\\n[tool bash -> success] args={\\\"command\\\":\\\"cd /Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components && cat > /tmp/survey.ts <<'E'\\\\nimport { parseCssDocs } from \\\\\\\"@cssdoc/core\\\\\\\";\\\\nimport { UTILITIES } from \\\\\\\"/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/utilities/index.ts\\\\\\\";\\\\nimport { RULES } from \\\\\\\"/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/rules/index.ts\\\\\\\";\\\\nimport { DECLARATIONS } from \\\\\\\"/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/declarations/index.ts\\\\\\\";\\\\nimport { resolveExampleTargets } from \\\\\\\"@pantoken/utils/example-targets\\\\\\\";\\\\nfor (const [k, list] of [[\\\\\\\"util\\\\\\\", UTILITIES], [\\\\\\\"rule\\\\\\\", RULES], [\\\\\\\"decl\\\\\\\", DECLARATIONS]] as const)\\\\n for (const r of list) {\\\\n const es = parseCssDocs(r.rules(\\\\\\\"instui-\\\\\\\")).filter((e) => e.name === r.name);\\\\n const e = es[0];\\\\n console.log(k, r.name, \\\\\\\"entries\\\\\\\", es.length, \\\\\\\"a11y\\\\\\\", !!e?.accessibility?.trim(), \\\\\\\"ex\\\\\\\", e?.examples.length, \\\\\\\"auto\\\\\\\", e ? resolveExampleTargets(e.examples).automatica11y.length : \\\\\\\"-\\\\\\\");\\\\n }\\\\nE\\\\ncp /tmp/survey.ts scripts/_survey.ts && node scripts/_survey.ts 2>&1 | tail -30; rm scripts/_survey.ts\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Survey utility/rule/declaration records\\\"}\\n[tool bash -> success] args={\\\"command\\\":\\\"cd /Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src && ls utilities/spacing utilities/transition utilities/truncate; sed -n 1,60p utilities/truncate/index.ts; sed -n 1,40p utilities/transition/transition.css; grep -n \\\\\\\"color\\\\\\\" ../scripts/generate.ts | head -20; sed -n 1,80p lib/define.ts | head -90\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"See how utility records are authored\\\"}\\n[tool bash -> success] args={\\\"command\\\":\\\"cd /Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/utilities && sed -n 10,60p truncate/index.ts; echo ======; sed -n 1,40p transition/transition.css\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Truncate and transition\\\"}\\n[tool bash -> success] args={\\\"command\\\":\\\"cd /Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken && grep -rn \\\\\\\"@utility color\\\\\\\\|@component color\\\\\\\\|--text-danger\\\\\\\" --include=*.ts formats/components/src formats/components/scripts -l | head; sed -n 1,30p docs/api/css/color.md | cut -c1-300\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Locate color record\\\"}\\n[tool bash -> success] args={\\\"command\\\":\\\"cd /Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components && grep -n \\\\\\\"@utility color\\\\\\\" -B12 -A25 scripts/generate.ts | head -90\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Color record in generate.ts\\\"}\\n[tool bash -> success] args={\\\"command\\\":\\\"cd /Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src && grep -n \\\\\\\"automatica11y\\\\\\\" -B6 -A8 utilities/icon/index.ts | head -40; for u in spacing gap layout responsive position overflow cursor stacking mask; do echo \\\\\\\"=== $u\\\\\\\"; grep -n \\\\\\\"@example\\\\\\\" -A6 utilities/$u/index.ts | head -14; done\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Existing authoring pattern and current examples\\\"}\\n[tool bash -> success] args={\\\"command\\\":\\\"cd /Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src && grep -rn '\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\`html' utilities rules | head -3; grep -n \\\\\\\"@example\\\\\\\" -B3 -A8 utilities/visual-debug/visual-debug.css rules/base/base.css | head -50; grep -n \\\\\\\"@a11y\\\\\\\\|@example\\\\\\\" rules/prose/*.ts rules/prose/*.css 2>/dev/null | head; ls rules/prose\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Fence escaping, base/visual-debug/prose\\\"}\\n[tool bash -> success] args={\\\"command\\\":\\\"cd /Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src && grep -rn '\\\\\\\"ai-gradient\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\|name: \\\\\\\"ai-gradient' . ../../../plugins/pantoken/*/src 2>/dev/null | head; sed -n 1,60p utilities/position/index.ts | grep -n \\\\\\\"position-\\\\\\\\|@modifier\\\\\\\" | head; grep -n \\\\\\\"@modifier\\\\\\\" utilities/stacking/index.ts utilities/layout/index.ts utilities/mask/index.ts | cut -c1-160 | head -30; sed -n 1,60p rules/prose/index.ts\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Check class names, prose, ai-gradient collision\\\"}\\n[tool bash -> success] args={\\\"command\\\":\\\"cd /Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken && cat formats/components/src/utilities/ai-gradient/index.ts | head -40; grep -rn \\\\\\\"ai-gradient\\\\\\\\|aiGradient\\\\\\\" formats/components/src --include=index.ts | grep -v \\\\\\\"utilities/ai-gradient/index.ts\\\\\\\" | head\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Core ai-gradient\\\"}\\n[tool edit -> success] args={\\\"path\\\":\\\"/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/utilities/truncate/index.ts\\\",\\\"old_str\\\":\\\" * @related text — Body typography that this truncates.\\\",\\\"new_str\\\":\\\" * @a11y Truncation hides overflowing text visually while it stays in the DOM, so don't clip information people need (titles, errors, instructions) and keep the full text available another way. Check that clipped text still reads correctly when zoomed or resized.\\\\n * @example -automatica11y\\\\n * \\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`html\\\\n * <p class=\\\\\\\"--truncate --max-lines-2\\\\\\\" style=\\\\\\\"inline-size: 16rem\\\\\\\">Quarterly planning notes for the curriculum review committee, including agenda items and follow-up actions.</p>\\\\n * \\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`\\\\n * @related text — Body typography that this truncates.\\\"}\\n[tool bash -> success] args={\\\"command\\\":\\\"cd /Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/utilities && for u in overflow spacing gap layout position stacking cursor mask; do echo \\\\\\\"=== $u\\\\\\\"; grep -n \\\\\\\"@example\\\\\\\" -B3 -A4 $u/index.ts | head -14; done; grep -n \\\\\\\"@modifier\\\\\\\" overflow/index.ts position/index.ts cursor/index.ts spacing/index.ts gap/index.ts | cut -c1-150 | head -30\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"View anchors for edits\\\"}\\n[tool edit -> success] args={\\\"new_str\\\":\\\" * @a11y A scrollable region must work from the keyboard: give it \\\\\\\\`tabindex=\\\\\\\"0\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\`, a role, and an accessible name (or make sure it contains a focusable control). Don't use \\\\\\\\`hidden\\\\\\\\` or \\\\\\\\`clip\\\\\\\\` to cut off content people need to read.\\\\n * @example -automatica11y\\\\n * \\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`html\\\\n * <div class=\\\\\\\"--overflow-y-auto\\\\\\\" tabindex=\\\\\\\"0\\\\\\\" role=\\\\\\\"region\\\\\\\" aria-label=\\\\\\\"Release notes\\\\\\\" style=\\\\\\\"block-size: 5rem\\\\\\\">\\\\n * <p>Version 2.4 adds keyboard shortcuts for the gradebook.</p>\\\\n * <p>Version 2.3 fixes focus order in the course menu.</p>\\\\n * <p>Version 2.2 improves contrast in dark mode.</p>\\\\n * <p>Version 2.1 updates the file upload messages.</p>\\\\n * </div>\\\\n * \\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`\\\\n * @example\\\\n * <div class=\\\\\\\"--overflow-y-auto\\\\\\\">…</div>\\\",\\\"old_str\\\":\\\" * @example\\\\n * <div class=\\\\\\\"--overflow-y-auto\\\\\\\">…</div>\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/utilities/overflow/index.ts\\\"}\\n[tool edit -> success] args={\\\"new_str\\\":\\\" * @a11y Spacing is visual only: use it to keep text and controls from crowding, not to convey structure — use headings, lists, and landmarks for that. Leave enough space around interactive targets for WCAG 2.5.8, and don't rely on fixed spacing that breaks when users increase text spacing.\\\\n * @example -automatica11y\\\\n * \\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`html\\\\n * <div class=\\\\\\\"--p-md --mt-lg\\\\\\\">\\\\n * <h2>Office hours</h2>\\\\n * <p>Mondays and Wednesdays, 2–4 pm.</p>\\\\n * </div>\\\\n * \\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`\\\\n * @example\\\\n * <div class=\\\\\\\"--p-md --mt-lg\\\\\\\">Padded box with a large top margin.</div>\\\",\\\"old_str\\\":\\\" * @example\\\\n * <div class=\\\\\\\"--p-md --mt-lg\\\\\\\">Padded box with a large top margin.</div>\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/utilities/spacing/index.ts\\\"}\\n[tool edit -> success] args={\\\"new_str\\\":\\\" * @a11y A gap changes spacing only; reading and focus order still follow the DOM. Keep gaps between interactive controls large enough to meet WCAG 2.5.8 target spacing.\\\\n * @example -automatica11y\\\\n * \\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`html\\\\n * <div class=\\\\\\\"--display-flex --gap-sm\\\\\\\">\\\\n * <button class=\\\\\\\"instui-button\\\\\\\">Save</button>\\\\n * <button class=\\\\\\\"instui-button\\\\\\\">Cancel</button>\\\\n * </div>\\\\n * \\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`\\\\n * @example\\\\n * <div class=\\\\\\\"--display-flex --gap-sm\\\\\\\">\\\",\\\"old_str\\\":\\\" * @example\\\\n * <div class=\\\\\\\"--display-flex --gap-sm\\\\\\\">\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/utilities/gap/index.ts\\\"}\\n[tool edit -> success] args={\\\"new_str\\\":\\\" * @a11y \\\\\\\\`--display-none\\\\\\\\` removes an element from the accessibility tree as well as the screen, so use it only for content nobody needs. Flex and grid layout can't reorder content for assistive tech; keep the DOM order meaningful, and don't center or justify long passages of text.\\\\n * @example -automatica11y\\\\n * \\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`html\\\\n * <div class=\\\\\\\"--display-flex --text-align-center\\\\\\\">\\\\n * <span>Course</span>\\\\n * <span>Grades</span>\\\\n * </div>\\\\n * \\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`\\\\n * @example\\\\n * <div class=\\\\\\\"--display-flex --text-align-center\\\\\\\">\\\",\\\"old_str\\\":\\\" * @example\\\\n * <div class=\\\\\\\"--display-flex --text-align-center\\\\\\\">\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/utilities/layout/index.ts\\\"}\\n[tool edit -> success] args={\\\"new_str\\\":\\\" * @a11y Positioning changes where content appears, not where it sits in the DOM: keep the visual order matching the reading and focus order, and don't let positioned content cover a focused control.\\\\n * @example -automatica11y\\\\n * \\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`html\\\\n * <div class=\\\\\\\"--position-relative\\\\\\\">\\\\n * <p>Positioned content stays in reading order.</p>\\\\n * </div>\\\\n * \\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`\\\\n * @example\\\\n * <div class=\\\\\\\"--position-relative\\\\\\\">…</div>\\\",\\\"old_str\\\":\\\" * @example\\\\n * <div class=\\\\\\\"--position-relative\\\\\\\">…</div>\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/utilities/position/index.ts\\\"}\\n[tool edit -> success] args={\\\"new_str\\\":\\\" * @a11y Stacking order is visual only: a layered surface that covers focusable content hides the focus indicator. Overlays that take over the page also need focus management and an accessible name.\\\\n * @example -automatica11y\\\\n * \\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`html\\\\n * <div class=\\\\\\\"--stack-above\\\\\\\">\\\\n * <p>Content raised above the default flow.</p>\\\\n * </div>\\\\n * \\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`\\\\n * @example\\\\n * <div class=\\\\\\\"--stack-topmost\\\\\\\">Always on top.</div>\\\",\\\"old_str\\\":\\\" * @example\\\\n * <div class=\\\\\\\"--stack-topmost\\\\\\\">Always on top.</div>\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/utilities/stacking/index.ts\\\"}\\n[tool edit -> success] args={\\\"new_str\\\":\\\" * @a11y The cursor only affects pointer users; a pointer cursor doesn't make an element operable. Put it on native controls (\\\\\\\\`button\\\\\\\\`, \\\\\\\\`a\\\\\\\\`), and never use \\\\\\\\`--cursor-not-allowed\\\\\\\\` or \\\\\\\\`--cursor-wait\\\\\\\\` as the only sign that something is disabled or busy.\\\\n * @example -automatica11y\\\\n * \\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`html\\\\n * <button class=\\\\\\\"instui-button --cursor-pointer\\\\\\\">Open details</button>\\\\n * \\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`\\\\n * @example\\\\n * <div class=\\\\\\\"--cursor-pointer\\\\\\\">…</div>\\\",\\\"old_str\\\":\\\" * @example\\\\n * <div class=\\\\\\\"--cursor-pointer\\\\\\\">…</div>\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/utilities/cursor/index.ts\\\"}\\n[tool edit -> success] args={\\\"new_str\\\":\\\" * @a11y A mask covers content visually but doesn't block assistive tech or the keyboard: make the covered region \\\\\\\\`inert\\\\\\\\` (or mark it \\\\\\\\`aria-busy\\\\\\\\`), keep the mask's own message as real text, and don't hide the focus indicator behind it.\\\\n * @example -automatica11y\\\\n * \\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`html\\\\n * <div class=\\\\\\\"--position-relative\\\\\\\" style=\\\\\\\"min-block-size: 4rem\\\\\\\">\\\\n * <p>Gradebook</p>\\\\n * <div class=\\\\\\\"--mask-overlay\\\\\\\" role=\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\">Loading grades…</div>\\\\n * </div>\\\\n * \\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`\\\\n * @example\\\\n * <button class=\\\\\\\"instui-button --mask-overlay\\\\\\\">…</button>\\\",\\\"old_str\\\":\\\" * @example\\\\n * <button class=\\\\\\\"instui-button --mask-overlay\\\\\\\">…</button>\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components/src/utilities/mask/index.ts\\\"}\\n[tool edit -> success] args={\\\"new_str\\\":\\\" * @a11y Hiding content at a breakpoint also hides it from assistive tech, so don't hide the only way to complete a task, and keep the shown and hidden versions equivalent in meaning.\\\\n * @example -automatica11y\\\\n * \\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`\\\\\\\\`html\\\\n * <p class=\\\\\\\"instui-hidden-max-sm\\\\\\\">The full course description appears on larger screens.</p>\\\\n * <p class=\\\\\\\"instui-show-min-sm\\\\\\\">The full course description appears on larger screens.</