{"type":"session.compaction_complete","data":{"success":true,"outcome":"applied","compactionAttemptId":"80249331-b76f-4f7d-ae28-b966d50a1899","preCompactionMessagesLength":267,"messagesRemoved":252,"summaryContent":"<overview>\nRepo: `thedannywahl/pantoken` (Vite+ monorepo; use the `vp` CLI only, never raw pnpm). Branch `add-automatica11y`, PR #239. The user told me to ignore other agents working in the repo. I commit only my own files by explicit path, as conventional commits with the trailer `Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>`. I add a changeset only for user-visible changes.\n\nThe work began with fixing a failing CI job (`component-accessibility`). It grew into reshaping the \"Accessibility audit\" that automatica11y findings inject into each component's CSS API page (`docs/api/css/*.md`, under `## Accessibility`). The current goal is to make every applicable record audited: custom-components plugin records (done) and now core utilities, rules and declarations (in progress). The user said the layouts plugin does not need coverage.\n</overview>\n\n<history>\n1. CI fix, `component-accessibility` run 40591517167.\n   - Cause: the `audit:accessibility` task lacked the full build graph.\n   - Fix: `dependsOn: [\"pantoken-root#build:all\"]` in `formats/components/vite.config.ts`, plus a test and a doc note.\n   - Commits `13a143443`, `2245df2cb`.\n\n2. User: append audit content, without its own header, to each component's `@accessibility`/`@a11y` block, and add blocks where missing.\n   - Added `@a11y` to 37 CSS records, merged the injector into the existing `## Accessibility` section, and added a guard test and a changeset.\n   - Commit `677e851e5`.\n\n3. User pasted a `vp fmt` error (plugin-kit dist missing). Rebuilt with `vp run @pantoken/plugin-kit#build`. Nothing to commit.\n\n4. User: removed the audit preamble (`bc7bdde87`).\n\n5. User: removed the download link, the \"Page and npm evidence aren't equivalent…\" paragraph and the \"Evidence details and review items\" section. Kept only the caveat \"These automated results do not establish that the page meets WCAG; manual review is still needed.\" (`b70fdd85d`).\n\n6. User: drop IBM and make WCAG-aligned tables per tier.\n   - Columns: Rebrand (light), Rebrand (dark), Canvas, Canvas High Contrast.\n   - Cells are instui-pills.\n   - Per-check `details` added to the snapshot importer (`95369c88f`).\n\n7. User: first column shows the check name, then `WCAG 2.2 N.N.N` on a second line. The name may wrap; pills must not (`75057bbfd`).\n\n8. User: pills are Pass / Fail / Not applicable / a review label, each with an icon (`248ec7f1f`).\n\n9. User: omit rows that are Not applicable in every column (`d44edeed5`).\n\n10. User: blend axe results into the WCAG tables, keeping IBM out. Added a \"Rules (axe-core)\" tier (`1d2de9e11`).\n\n11. User: failing or review rows should span two rows, with a details row spanning all themes.\n    - Implemented as raw HTML tables (`<table class=\"pantoken-a11y-table\">`) with `rowspan=\"2\"`.\n    - Added `notes`.\n    - Commit `1ddaa334a`.\n\n12. User: rename \"Manual review needed\" to \"Review needed\" (`8f5c0e787`).\n\n13. User, about the avatar `color-contrast` review: it should be clear which variant caused it, for ALL components.\n    - Added the affected element to the details, first as markup (`614f1760f`, `c07353de6`).\n    - Then as a bulleted list of `<code>` items via a new `elements` field (`3f783df32`).\n    - Then as axe's selector, e.g. `.-color-ai`, rather than the full markup (`348ca2e55`).\n    - I explained that mapping selectors to cssdoc `@modifier`/`@part` names would be possible but would couple the importer to the component records. The user did not request it.\n\n14. User: agent-shell shows \"not audited\"; all components should be audited.\n    - I asked about scope. The user chose \"custom-components only\".\n    - Created `formats/components/scripts/audit-plugin-components.ts`, which exports `PLUGIN_AUDIT_RECORDS` (agent-shell, banner, button-set, logo, segmented-control, skeleton-loader) and `PLUGIN_STYLESHEET`.\n    - `audit-accessibility.ts`:\n      - renders pages with the plugin stylesheet;\n      - copies `plugins/pantoken/custom-components/dist` to `assets/custom-components`;\n      - `runPageAudits` uses `[...COMPONENTS, focus, ...PLUGIN_AUDIT_RECORDS]`.\n    - Added `@a11y` and an `-automatica11y` example to `agent-shell.css`.\n    - Added a plugin guard test and updated the orchestrator tests.\n    - Ran the full audit (run dir `a11y-report/2026-10-28T18-16-06.299Z`, about 50 minutes) and re-imported it. The snapshot went from 76 to 82 records.\n    - Added changeset `.changeset/audit-custom-components.md` for `@pantoken/plugin-custom-components` (patch).\n    - Commits `354527dd2`, `0ab3c292a`, `ea78abf32`. The checked-in snapshot test was updated to 82 records, with `agent-shell` present and `ai-gradient` undefined.\n\n15. User (latest): layouts plugin needn't be covered. For both components and custom-components, go through the utilities, declarations, etc. and add audits where applicable.\n    - Surveyed which records lack `@a11y` or an automatica11y example.\n    - Edited the sources (below). Not yet wired into the audit, tested, or committed.\n</history>\n\n<work_done>\nCommitted (all mine): everything through `ea78abf32`.\n\nUncommitted edits for request 15. All add `@a11y` text and a fenced `-automatica11y` HTML example before the existing `@example`. In the TS records, backticks and fences are escaped as `\\`` / `\\`\\`\\`html`.\n\n- `formats/components/src/utilities/`:\n  - `truncate/index.ts`\n  - `overflow/index.ts` (focusable scroll region example)\n  - `spacing/index.ts`\n  - `gap/index.ts`\n  - `layout/index.ts`\n  - `position/index.ts`\n  - `stacking/index.ts`\n  - `cursor/index.ts`\n  - `mask/index.ts` (the record named `maskglobal`)\n  - `responsive/index.ts`\n  - `ai-gradient/index.ts` (the core record)\n- Example only, since `@a11y` already existed: `utilities/transition/transition.css`, `utilities/visual-debug/visual-debug.css`, `rules/base/base.css`.\n- `rules/prose/index.ts`: both `@a11y` and the example added.\n\nNOT done yet:\n- Wire these records into the audit. `UTILITIES`, `RULES` and `aiGradient` need to be added to the `definitions` in `runPageAudits` and `runNpmAudits`, deduplicated by name.\n- Extend the guard tests.\n- Run lint and tests.\n- Re-run the full audit and re-import.\n- Update the snapshot-count test.\n- Add a changeset and commit.\n</work_done>\n\n<technical_details>\n- Audit data flow:\n  - `formats/components/scripts/audit-accessibility.ts` writes `a11y-report/<run>`.\n  - `docs/scripts/accessibility-evidence.ts` imports it: `vp exec node docs/scripts/accessibility-evidence.ts a11y-report/<run>`.\n  - That produces `docs/public/accessibility/results.json`.\n  - `docs/scripts/build-css-api.ts` calls `annotateAccessibility`. Regenerate pages with `vp run @pantoken/docs#docs:api:css`; the pages are gitignored.\n  - `vp run … modified its inputs` is the normal message.\n- Audit commands, run from `formats/components`:\n  - `node scripts/audit-accessibility.ts [--record name]`. A single record takes about 40 s; the full run takes about 50 minutes (use an async shell and read in 600 s waits).\n  - Each record needs exactly one cssdoc entry with that name, and at least one `-automatica11y` example (`resolveExampleTargets(...).automatica11y`).\n  - `exampleHtml` converts `pfx-` to `instui-`. Examples in core records must use literal `instui-`; the guard test forbids `pfx-` in core records.\n- Core record registries:\n  - `COMPONENTS` already includes `icon` and `screen-reader-content` (also in `UTILITIES`, so dedupe by name).\n  - `UTILITIES` has: spacing, gap, layout, responsive, position, overflow, cursor, stacking, maskglobal, icon, screen-reader-content, transition, truncate, visual-debug.\n  - `RULES` has base and prose.\n  - `DECLARATIONS` has focus and elevation. `focus` is already audited.\n  - `ai-gradient` is NOT in `UTILITIES`; import `aiGradient` from `src/utilities/ai-gradient/index.ts` directly. The plugin-custom-components package has its own `ai-gradient` record with the same name. Only one can be audited, so audit the core one.\n- Decided not applicable or skipped:\n  - elevation (shadow, no markup);\n  - breakpoints (preview widths);\n  - segmented-control.segment (member, covered by its parent);\n  - primitives (plugin, arbitrary palette);\n  - the layouts plugin (per user);\n  - logos.\n- `color` is a generated doc block (`colorDoc` in `formats/components/scripts/generate.ts`, with `@utility color` and `.--text-danger`). It would need its `@a11y` and example added there, and a way to feed it to the audit. generate.ts executes on import, so it's awkward. I had not decided; mention it to the user.\n- `vp check` enforces `tsdoc-require` (exported consts need TSDoc).\n- Pre-commit runs `vp staged`. If it fails on a missing module, build the dependency (for example `vp run @pantoken/utils#build`).\n- The edit tool is fragile with overlapping or re-used `old_str`, and it can silently match a partial line. After multi-edit batches on one file, verify with `git diff`. Avoid sed or python for file changes.\n- Renderer details:\n  - A cell's status is the worst result across the page and npm evidence: fail > review > pass > not-applicable.\n  - HTML tables are not translated by the segmenter (HTML blocks are preserved verbatim). Blocks must contain no blank lines.\n  - Escaping inside raw HTML uses `html()`.\n- The snapshot stores `details` (tier, name, criteria, counts, `notes`, `elements`). `elements` are axe selectors, up to 5, each cut at 80 characters.\n- Remaining uncommitted files belonging to other agents, not to be staged: `l10n/docs.api.pot`, and an `avatar.css` formatting diff (`> img` → `>img`).\n- Remote CI hasn't been re-run on any of these changes. The rendered output hasn't been viewed in a browser.\n</technical_details>\n\n<important_files>\n- `formats/components/scripts/audit-accessibility.ts`\n  - Audit orchestrator. Contains `renderPage`, `runPageAudits`, `runNpmAudits` and the asset copy list. It currently builds definitions from `[...COMPONENTS, focus, ...PLUGIN_AUDIT_RECORDS]`.\n  - `runNpmAudits` (around line 552) uses `[...COMPONENTS, focus]` for archetypes only; that is probably fine to leave.\n- `formats/components/scripts/audit-plugin-components.ts`\n  - Plugin record list and stylesheet constant. Extend or pair it with the core utility, rule and aiGradient list.\n- `formats/components/tests/audit-examples.test.ts`\n  - Guard tests: `@a11y` text and an automatica11y example exist. It already has a plugin-records test, and now needs a similar one for the newly audited utilities and rules.\n- `formats/components/tests/audit-accessibility.test.ts`\n  - Orchestrator fixtures. They need the `plugins/pantoken/custom-components/dist` directory, and the expected assets listing `[\"assets\",\"components\",\"custom-components\",\"interactions\",\"tokens\"]`.\n- `docs/scripts/accessibility-evidence.ts` / `.test.ts`\n  - Importer and renderer. The test asserts the snapshot has 82 records (agent-shell present, ai-gradient undefined). It must be updated after the next audit.\n- `docs/public/accessibility/results.json`\n  - Checked-in snapshot.\n- `docs/.vitepress/i18n.ts`\n  - Pill and audit strings (`review: \"Review needed\"`, `noResult`, `notAudited`).\n- `docs/.vitepress/theme/pantoken.css`\n  - `.pantoken-a11y-*` styles.\n- `docs/conventions/build-and-docs.md`\n  - Audit docs. Mention the extra audited record groups if relevant.\n- The utility, rule and component sources edited above, plus `plugins/pantoken/custom-components/src/components/agent-shell/agent-shell.css`.\n- `.changeset/audit-custom-components.md`: the existing changeset. Add another for `@pantoken/components` (patch) covering the new utility and rule guidance and examples.\n</important_files>\n\n<next_steps>\nRemaining work:\n- Wire the core records into the audit:\n  - Import `UTILITIES`, `RULES` and `aiGradient`.\n  - Build a deduped-by-name definition list, shared between `runPageAudits` and the guard tests.\n  - Confirm `maskglobal` (`maskUtility`) has a single entry with that name.\n- Extend the guard test to cover the new record groups: `@a11y` text plus an automatica11y example, with unique ids and no `pfx-`.\n- Run `vp check --fix formats/components docs`, then the audit and docs tests:\n  - `vp test run formats/components/tests/audit-accessibility.test.ts formats/components/tests/audit-examples.test.ts docs/scripts`\n  - Also run the components tests that validate record docs, and the generate parity or snapshot tests that may be affected by doc-comment changes (check for failures).\n- Smoke-test one or two records (for example `--record truncate` and `--record base`) before the full run.\n- Run the full audit (async, about 50 minutes). Import the run directory, regenerate the API pages, and verify the pages for the newly audited records show tables.\n- Update the snapshot-count assertion in `docs/scripts/accessibility-evidence.test.ts`.\n- Add a changeset for `@pantoken/components`.\n- Commit in increments, staging by explicit path and with the trailer:\n  - the source docs and examples;\n  - the audit wiring and tests;\n  - the snapshot refresh;\n  - the changeset.\n\nReport to the user:\n- What is now audited.\n- What was skipped and why: elevation, breakpoints, primitives, segmented-control.segment, color (needs the `generate.ts` doc block and a way to feed it to the audit; ask whether to pursue it), and the layouts plugin.\n- The plugin `ai-gradient` and the core `ai-gradient` share a name, so only the core one is audited.\n- Remote CI has not been run, and the rendered pages have not been viewed in a browser.\n- `l10n/docs.api.pot` still needs regenerating (another agent has it modified).\n- HTML audit tables are not translated.\n</next_steps>\n\n<checkpoint_title>Auditing utilities and custom components</checkpoint_title>","behaviorModelId":"claude-sonnet-5.5","tokenLimit":200000,"trigger":"threshold","preCompactionTokens":144799,"postCompactionTokens":40910,"tokensRemoved":103889,"tokenAccountingBasis":"local_full_context_estimate","systemTokens":19609,"conversationTokens":10049,"toolDefinitionsTokens":11248,"responsesReasoning":{"model":"gpt-6.1-sol","initialEffort":"medium","effort":"medium"},"compactionTokensUsed":{"requestCount":1,"aiCreditsStatus":"complete","provider":{"id":"copilot","kind":"copilot","label":"GitHub Copilot"},"modelDisplayName":"Claude Sonnet 5.5","inputTokens":163381,"outputTokens":5404,"cacheReadTokens":159836,"cacheWriteTokens":3541,"copilotUsage":{"tokenDetails":[{"batchSize":1000000,"costPerBatch":180000000000,"model":"claude-sonnet-5.5","tokenCount":4,"tokenType":"input"},{"batchSize":1000000,"costPerBatch":9000000000,"model":"claude-sonnet-5.5","tokenCount":159836,"tokenType":"cache_read"},{"batchSize":1000000,"costPerBatch":225000000000,"model":"claude-sonnet-5.5","tokenCount":3541,"tokenType":"cache_write"},{"batchSize":1000000,"costPerBatch":900000000000,"model":"claude-sonnet-5.5","tokenCount":5404,"tokenType":"output"}],"totalNanoAiu":7099569000},"duration":34313,"model":"claude-sonnet-5.5"},"requestId":"9AA3:A5345:37222A5:3A47BBC:6AE248A8","serviceRequestId":"e38aac07-8365-4d28-a8f0-3424e59b7332","checkpointNumber":3,"checkpointPath":"/Users/dwahl/.copilot/session-state/cf8db52f-0f27-4d51-8f45-3f9af32eb056/checkpoints/003-auditing-utilities-and-custom.md"},"id":"70aee47e-9c0e-461f-ae9c-689a6b271b0a","timestamp":"2026-10-28T19:11:12.237Z","parentId":"9dfa0382-a90a-44f5-b77b-91054123b0a7"}
